            {
              "tool_call_id": "call_Hm0ef5kcw8GfGm9AJmbOBSdu",
              "status": "success",
              "stdout": null,
              "stderr": null,
              "func_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"OK\",\n  \"message\": \"{\\n  \\\"api_key_source\\\": \\\"system_settings\\\",\\n  \\\"results\\\": {\\n    \\\"Letta Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error\\\": {\\n      \\\"query\\\": \\\"Letta Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error\\\",\\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"What are possible solutions for the error 'There was an error attaching this tool, please try again or contact support.'?\\\",\\n      \\\"raw_results\\\": {\\n        \\\"success\\\": true,\\n        \\\"data\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"title\\\": \\\"Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool · Issue #2521\\\",\\n            \\\"description\\\": \\\"Describe the bug Tool created with the error raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\"Something went wrong - we should never be using the persisted source code for MCP.\\\",\\n            \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521\\\",\\n            \\\"markdown\\\": \\\"[Skip to content](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#start-of-content)\\\\n\\\\n[letta-ai](https://github.com/letta-ai)/ **[letta](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta)** Public\\\\n\\\\n- [Notifications](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta) You must be signed in to change notification settings\\\\n- [Fork\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1.9k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\\\n- [Star\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n17.7k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n# Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool\\\\\\\\#2521\\\\n\\\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\\\n\\\\nCopy link\\\\n\\\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\\\n\\\\nCopy link\\\\n\\\\nClosed\\\\n\\\\nClosed\\\\n\\\\n[Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#top)#2521\\\\n\\\\nCopy link\\\\n\\\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\n## Description\\\\n\\\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\n[Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\nopened [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#issue-2946746710)\\\\n\\\\nIssue body actions\\\\n\\\\n**Describe the bug**\\\\n\\\\nTool created with the error\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\"Something went wrong - we should never be using the persisted source code for MCP. Please reach out to Letta team\\\\\\\")\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Please describe your setup**\\\\n\\\\nDocker Compose file with following setup\\\\n\\\\n```notranslate\\\\nversion: \\\\\\\"3.8\\\\\\\"\\\\nservices:\\\\n  letta:\\\\n    image: letta/letta:latest\\\\n    ports:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"8283:8283\\\\\\\"\\\\n    volumes:\\\\n      - ~/.letta/.persist/pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data\\\\n      - ./mcp_config.json:/root/.letta/mcp_config.json\\\\n    depends_on:\\\\n      python-setup:\\\\n        condition: service_healthy\\\\n\\\\n  python-setup:\\\\n    build: .\\\\n    container_name: fast_mpc\\\\n    ports:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3000:3000\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"5173:5173\\\\\\\"\\\\n    command: [\\\\\\\"mcp\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"main.py\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    healthcheck:\\\\n      test: [\\\\\\\"CMD\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"curl\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"-f\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"http://localhost:5173\\\\\\\"]\\\\n      interval: 10s\\\\n      timeout: 5s\\\\n      retries: 5\\\\n      start_period: 10s\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nA main.py file containing the MCP example code\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nfrom mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\\\\n\\\\nmcp = FastMCP(\\\\\\\"Demo\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n@mcp.tool()\\\\ndef add(a: int, b: int) -> int:\\\\n    return a + b\\\\n\\\\n@mcp.resource(\\\\\\\"greeting://{name}\\\\\\\")\\\\ndef get_greeting(name: str) -> str:\\\\n    return f\\\\\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nif __name__ == \\\\\\\"__main__\\\\\\\":\\\\n    mcp.run()\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nA docker container that acts as the server\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nFROM python:3.11\\\\n\\\\nCOPY ./main.py /code/main.py\\\\nCOPY ./poetry.lock /code/poetry.lock\\\\nCOPY ./pyproject.toml /code/pyproject.toml\\\\n\\\\nWORKDIR /code\\\\n\\\\nRUN apt-get update && \\\\\\\\\\\\n    apt-get install -y curl && \\\\\\\\\\\\n    curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_18.x | bash - && \\\\\\\\\\\\n    apt-get install -y nodejs\\\\n\\\\nRUN npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@0.6.0\\\\n\\\\nRUN pip install poetry\\\\nRUN poetry self add poetry-plugin-export\\\\nRUN poetry export -o requirements.txt --without-hashes\\\\nRUN poetry config virtualenvs.create false\\\\nRUN poetry install\\\\nRUN pip install mcp[cli]\\\\n\\\\nCMD [\\\\\\\"python\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"main.py\\\\\\\"]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nMCP config\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"mcpServers\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"localTools\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://python-setup:3000/sse?transportType=stdio&command=python&args=main.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nOnce running I executed the following script\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nimport os\\\\n\\\\nfrom letta_client import Letta\\\\n\\\\nos.environ[\\\\\\\"LETTA_URL\\\\\\\"] = \\\\\\\"http://localhost:8283\\\\\\\"\\\\nletta_url = os.getenv(\\\\\\\"LETTA_URL\\\\\\\")\\\\nclient = Letta(base_url=letta_url)\\\\n\\\\nservers = client.tools.list_mcp_servers()\\\\nfor server in servers:\\\\n    mcp_tools = client.tools.list_mcp_tools_by_server(mcp_server_name=server)\\\\n    for tool in mcp_tools:\\\\n        tool_res = client.tools.add_mcp_tool(mcp_server_name=server, mcp_tool_name=tool.name)\\\\n        res = client.agents.tools.attach(agent_id=\\\\\\\"agent-2ea95cad-1c00-4930-a8ce-369f10d33f0e\\\\\\\", tool_id=tool_res.id)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Screenshots**\\\\n\\\\n[![Image](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52256942/426574738-43b29574-3bed-4a8b-9714-9ec1c1065778.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..A_mNR-M5QhvKzK5L_vjxaAQofM-1K63SXtrMwFXKPrI)](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52256942/426574738-43b29574-3bed-4a8b-9714-9ec1c1065778.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..A_mNR-M5QhvKzK5L_vjxaAQofM-1K63SXtrMwFXKPrI)\\\\n\\\\n## Activity\\\\n\\\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\\\n\\\\nadded this to [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#event-16975883292)\\\\n\\\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\\\n\\\\nmoved this to To triage in [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\\\n\\\\n[![Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\n### Jonathan-Harker commented on Mar 28, 2025\\\\n\\\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\n[Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\n[on Mar 28, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#issuecomment-2762022390)\\\\n\\\\nAuthor\\\\n\\\\nFixed many thanks\\\\n\\\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?s=64&u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4)Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\\\n\\\\nclosed this as [completed](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aclosed%20archived%3Af