        {
          "type": "message",
          "role": "user",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "[Recent conversation context:]\n- cameron_pfiffer: As a general request, please reach out to us if you run into any unexpected behavior with the V1 SDK. It's been a big undertaking and we may need to do some bug squashing.\n\nPost any bug reports in <#1162177332350558339> and I'll start tracking tickets.\n- devid.johnas: Lately I’ve been deep into building voice agents and the hardest parts have been latency, call handoffs, and clean event control during live conversations.\n\nCurious, how are you guys handling things like real-time call flows and structured summaries?\nRight now I’m using [Feather AI](<https://www.featherhq.com/?utm_source=reddit&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=feather&utm_content=comment>)  for this and so far it’s been solid for:\nsub-second latency\n\n-> stable agent logic even if users go off-script\n\n-> clean transcription + event streams\n\n-> pushing results into CRMs reliably\n\nStill experimenting and learning, so if anyone has better setups, tools, or architectures they’ve tried, would love to hear.\n- hao_bai: Looking for Letta Lite APK for Android to import ADE agent (.af file)”（其实我不会英文，你找我可能我注意不到..）\n- legal0999: looking for to build stateful AI agents\n- d_c9753: Are you associated with them?\n- cameron_pfiffer: it's giving that vibe\n[End context]\n\n[cameron_pfiffer (id=657626741854044220) sent a message in #💬｜general] you are in the correct place\n\n[IMPORTANT: You are only observing this message. You cannot respond in this channel. Your response will not be sent to Discord.]",
              "signature": null
            }
          ],
