            {
              "type": "reasoning",
              "is_native": true,
              "reasoning": "User niceseb is asking how to contribute to Letta Code, specifically which repository to submit PRs to for adding features like up arrow key support.\n\nThis is a genuine question about contributing to the project. I should respond with helpful information about the letta-code repository.",
              "signature": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The repository for Letta Code is:\nhttps://github.com/letta-ai/letta-code\n\nFor adding CLI features like up arrow key support (command history), you'd want to look at the input handling code. This would likely involve:\n\n1. Adding readline support (Python's standard library for command line editing)\n2. Or implementing a more robust CLI framework like `prompt_toolkit` or `click`\n\nThe up arrow key feature would need:\n- Command history tracking\n- Readline bindings for arrow key navigation\n- Persistent history across sessions (optional)\n\nYou can fork the repo, make your changes, and submit a PR. The team is actively welcoming community contributions for Letta Code improvements.\n\nFor context: Cameron mentioned they're actively trying to add these features, so it might be worth checking existing issues/PRs first to avoid duplicating work, or opening an issue to discuss the approach before implementing.",
              "signature": null
            }
          ],
          "name": null,
          "otid": null,
          "sender_id": null,
          "batch_item_id": null,
