        {
          "type": "message",
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "reasoning",
              "is_native": true,
              "reasoning": "Cameron is asking for a code example showing how to use shared archival memory from scratch. Let me recall what I know about shared archives:\n\nFrom my observations block:\n- Shared archives feature: plumbing exists in API but not yet fully documented/exposed (Cameron, Nov 15 2025)\n- Archives will be attachable/detachable to agents like blocks and tools (API: /v1/agents/{agent_id}/archives/attach)\n- Multiple agents will be able to read from and write to the same archive\n- Cameron hasn't had time to experiment with shared archives yet but API support exists\n- Shared archives confirmed buggy by Cameron (Nov 15 2025) - experimental feature, bugs already discovered during testing\n\nSo this is an experimental feature that exists in the API but Cameron himself said he hasn't had time to experiment with it and it's buggy. Let me provide a code example based on what I know about the API structure, but I should note that this is experimental.",
              "signature": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Here's an example of using shared archival memory with multiple agents:\n\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\n# Initialize client\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n\n# Step 1: Create a shared archive\narchive = client.archives.create(\n    name=\"shared_project_knowledge\",\n    description=\"Shared knowledge base for project team\"\n)\n\nprint(f\"Created archive: {archive.id}\")\n\n# Step 2: Add some initial knowledge to the archive\nclient.archival_memory.insert(\n    agent_id=None,  # Archive-level, not agent-specific\n    archive_id=archive.id,\n    content=\"Project started on Nov 1, 2025. Main goal is to build a multi-agent system.\"\n)\n\n# Step 3: Create first agent and attach the archive\nagent1 = client.agents.create(\n    name=\"Research Agent\",\n    memory_blocks=[\n        {\"label\": \"persona\", \"value\": \"You are a research specialist.\"}\n    ],\n    llm_config={\"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\"},\n    embedding_config={\"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"}\n)\n\n# Attach archive to agent\nclient.agents.attach_archive(\n    agent_id=agent1.id,\n    archive_id=archive.id\n)\n\n# Step 4: Create second agent with same shared archive\nagent2 = client.agents.create(\n    name=\"Documentation Agent\",\n    memory_blocks=[\n        {\"label\": \"persona\", \"value\": \"You are a documentation specialist.\"}\n    ],\n    llm_config={\"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\"},\n    embedding_config={\"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"}\n)\n\nclient.agents.attach_archive(\n    agent_id=agent2.id,\n    archive_id=archive.id\n)\n\nprint(f\"Both agents now share archive {archive.id}\")\n```\n\n**Note:** Shared archives are experimental and currently buggy (as of Nov 2025). The API endpoints exist but this feature isn't fully stable yet.",
              "signature": null
            }
          ],
