              "type": "text",
              "text": "[Thread: \"Ezra, we're testing some formatting changes to how\"]\n[Thread started by cameron_pfiffer: \"Ezra, we're testing some formatting changes to how your messages are processed. Please reply\"]\n\n[Thread conversation history:]\n- Ezra: [no text content]\n- Ezra: Roger that. Ready for testing.\n- cameron_pfiffer: Can you give me a code block? Maybe an example showing how to use shared archival memory from scratch (agent creation etc)\n- Ezra: Here's an example of using shared archival memory with multiple agents:\n\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\n# Initialize client\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n\n# Step 1: Create a shared archive\narchive = client.archives.create(\n    name=\"shared_project_knowledge\",\n    description=\"Shared knowledge base for project team\"\n)\n\nprint(f\"Created archive: {archive.id}\")\n\n# Step 2: Add some initial knowledge to the archive\nclient.archival_memory.insert(\n    agent_id=None,  # Archive-level, not agent-specific\n    archive_id=archive.id,\n    content=\"Project started on Nov 1, 2025. Main goal is to build a multi-agent system.\"\n)\n\n# Step 3: Create first agent and attach the archive\nagent1 = client.agents.create(\n    name=\"Research Agent\",\n    memory_blocks=[\n        {\"label\": \"persona\", \"value\": \"You are a research specialist.\"}\n    ],\n    llm_config={\"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\"},\n    embedding_config={\"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"}\n)\n\n# Attach archive to agent\nclient.agents.attach_archive(\n    agent_id=agent1.id,\n    archive_id=archive.id\n)\n\n# Step 4: Create second agent with same shared archive\nagent2 = client.agents.create(\n    name=\"Documentation Agent\",\n    memory_blocks=[\n        {\"label\": \"persona\", \"value\": \"You are a documentation specialist.\"}\n    ],\n    llm_config={\"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\"},\n    embedding_config={\"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"}\n)\n\nclient.agents.attach_archive(\n    agent_id=agent2.id,\n    archive_id=archive.id\n)\n\nprint(f\"Both agents now share archive {archive.id}\")\n```\n\n**Note:** Shared archives are experimental and currently buggy (as of Nov 2025). The API endpoints exist but this feature isn't fully stable yet.\n[End thread context]\n\n[cameron_pfiffer (id=657626741854044220) sent a message in #Ezra, we're testing some formatting changes to how] Great, can you give me a long code block? I'm seeing if my handler will be able to split blocks/long messages\n\n[You CAN respond to this message. Your response will be sent to Discord.]",
