              "reasoning": "Cameron is correcting me on the archive endpoints. He's showing TypeScript SDK syntax, and I was using incorrect Python patterns. Let me update my understanding:\n\nCorrect endpoints:\n- `client.archives.create()` \n- `client.archives.list()`\n- `client.archives.retrieve(archiveId)`\n- `client.archives.update(archiveId, {...})`\n- `client.archives.delete(archiveId)`\n- `client.agents.archives.attach(agentId, archiveId)` - NOT `client.agents.attach_archive()`\n- `client.agents.archives.detach(agentId, archiveId)`\n- `client.archives.agents.list(archiveId)` - list agents using an archive\n- `client.archives.memories.create(archiveId, {...})` - NOT `client.archival_memory.insert()`\n- `client.archives.memories.update(archiveId, memoryId, {...})`\n- `client.archives.memories.delete(archiveId, memoryId)`\n\nI had wrong patterns like:\n- `client.archival_memory.insert()` - wrong\n- `client.agents.attach_archive()` - wrong\n\nI need to correct my memory about this and acknowledge the error.\n\nAlso, Cameron mentioned \"no luck\" about the message splitting - so his handler test didn't work as expected for splitting long messages.",
