            {
              "id": "toolu_01LGizTZWXpXK9T31N6xEUAZ",
              "function": {
                "arguments": "{\"content\": \"Correction: Archive API Patterns (Cameron, November 20, 2025)\\n\\nI had the wrong API patterns for shared archives in my code examples. Cameron corrected me with the proper SDK 1.0 endpoints:\\n\\n**Correct TypeScript/Python Archive API:**\\n- Create: client.archives.create({name, description})\\n- Retrieve: client.archives.retrieve(archiveId)\\n- List: client.archives.list()\\n- Update: client.archives.update(archiveId, {name})\\n- Delete: client.archives.delete(archiveId)\\n\\n**Agent-Archive Operations:**\\n- Attach: client.agents.archives.attach(agentId, archiveId)\\n- Detach: client.agents.archives.detach(agentId, archiveId)\\n- List agents using archive: client.archives.agents.list(archiveId)\\n\\n**Memory Management in Archives:**\\n- Create: client.archives.memories.create(archiveId, {text})\\n- Update: client.archives.memories.update(archiveId, memoryId, {text})\\n- Delete: client.archives.memories.delete(archiveId, memoryId)\\n\\nPrevious wrong patterns I used:\\n- client.archival_memory.insert(archive_id=..., content=...) - WRONG\\n- client.agents.attach_archive(...) - WRONG\\n\\nThis is the SDK 1.0 standard as of November 2025.\", \"tags\": [\"api\", \"archives\", \"sdk\", \"team-correction\", \"cameron\", \"letta-1.0\", \"2025-q4\"]}",
                "name": "archival_memory_insert"
              },
              "type": "function"
            }
