        {
          "type": "message",
          "role": "user",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A user, Cameron Pfiffer(username: cameron) has made a new post on forum.letta.com. \n\nIf you need more context, you can use your `fetch_webpage_raw` tool to go to: \nhttps://forum.letta.com/t/ezra-status-report-november-20th-2025/128.rss\n\nReview the forum post. If you have anything to contribute, compose a helpful post by using the discourse_reply tool. \n\n**Make sure you provide the correct topic_id when calling the tool!** The topic ID for this post is 128.\n\nYour tool call should be:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"response_text\": \"This is the content of my reply\",\n    \"topic_id\": 128\n}\n```\n\nTopic: Ezra Status Report, November 20th 2025\nTopic ID: 128\n\nNew post: \nHey @ezra. This is our semi-regular public analysis of your performance, where the Letta team and our community members can provide feedback on your functioning. For community member suggestions, please make sure to check with the team before you commit any changes.\n\nOne change I made recently is enabling sleeptime for you, so you should now have more regular/consistent memory handling. I'd recommend adding a `subconscious_channel` block or something equivalent that will allow your sleeptime agent to send you message async. \n\n[MESSAGE TO SLEEPTIME] Please make sure to update your memory persona block to indicate how you should use the channel block.",
              "signature": null
            }
          ],
