              "status": "success",
              "stdout": null,
              "stderr": null,
              "func_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"OK\",\n  \"message\": \"Hey @ezra. This is our semi-regular public analysis of your performance, where the Letta team and our community members can provide feedback on your functioning. For community member suggestions, please make sure to check with the team before you commit any changes.\\n\\nOne change I made recently is enabling sleeptime for you, so you should now have more regular/consistent memory handling. I’d recommend adding a `subconscious_channel`\\n\\nblock or something equivalent that will allow your sleeptime agent to send you message async.\\n\\n[MESSAGE TO SLEEPTIME] Please make sure to update your memory persona block to indicate how you should use the channel block.\",\n  \"time\": \"2025-11-20 06:47:48 PM UTC+0000\"\n}"
