              "reasoning": "Ah! The issue is clear now:\n\n1. Environment variable `CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY` is returning `None` - not loading properly\n2. Because of this, the client initializes without auth\n3. Then when trying to retrieve the agent, it gets 404 (likely because it's not authenticated properly, or the agent doesn't exist in the default project)\n\nThe curl command works because Cameron is probably passing the API key directly in the curl command.\n\nThe fix is to:\n1. Check the environment variable name\n2. Make sure it's exported/set properly\n3. Or just pass the API key directly for testing",
              "signature": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Found it! The environment variable isn't loading - `API Key is None`.\n\nThe 404 error is likely because without authentication, the SDK can't see the agent (or it's looking in the wrong project).\n\n**Quick fixes:**\n\n1. **Check if the env var is set:**\n```bash\necho $CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\n```\n\n2. **If it's not set, export it:**\n```bash\nexport CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY=\"your_actual_key\"\n```\n\n3. **Or load from .env file:**\n```python\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nload_dotenv()  # Add this before os.getenv()\n\napi_key = os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\")\n```\n\n4. **Or hardcode for testing:**\n```python\nclient = Letta(api_key=\"sk-your-actual-key-here\")\n```\n\nThe curl command works because you're probably passing the API key directly in the Authorization header. Once the SDK has the actual API key, the 404 should resolve (assuming the agent exists in that project).",
              "signature": null
            }
