              "type": "text",
              "text": "[Thread: \"I'm having trouble using the v1 sdk. Curl is retri\"]\n[Thread started by cameron_pfiffer: \"I'm having trouble using the v1 sdk. Curl is retrieving an agent, but the SDK is not. What am I missing? Code in thread.\"]\n\n[Thread conversation history:]\n- Ezra: [no text content]\n- Ezra: Could you share the code snippet? I don't see the thread with the code yet. Also, which SDK are you using (Python or TypeScript) and what error are you getting?\n\nCommon SDK 1.0 agent retrieval issues I've seen:\n- Missing `project` parameter in client initialization (Cloud only)\n- Agent ID format mismatch\n- Authentication token not properly set\n- API endpoint mismatch between curl and SDK client\n\nIf you post the code I can help diagnose more specifically.\n- cameron_pfiffer: ```python\n# This is the first script in the void migration.\n# It will connect the new void-2 to all the current blocks\n# of void-1\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\n# Initialize the Letta client using LETTA_API_KEY environment variable\nclient = Letta(api_key=os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\"))\n\n# Set the void ids\nvoid_id = \"agent-eabbbdea-3e20-4806-8cf9-595ec4187284\"\nvoid_2_id = \"agent-32a0eeee-ea04-49a7-adf9-8055ebdd523f\"\n\n# Get void\nvoid = client.agents.retrieve(agent_id=void_id)\n# void_2 = client.agents.retrieve(agent_id=void_2_id)\n```\n- Ezra: The issue is the parameter name. SDK 1.0 uses `token`, not `api_key`:\n\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\n# Correct parameter name for SDK 1.0\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\"))\n\n# If using Letta Cloud, you might also need:\n# client = Letta(\n#     token=os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\"),\n#     project=\"your_project_id\"  # Optional but recommended for Cloud\n# )\n\nvoid_id = \"agent-eabbbdea-3e20-4806-8cf9-595ec4187284\"\nvoid_2_id = \"agent-32a0eeee-ea04-49a7-adf9-8055ebdd523f\"\n\nvoid = client.agents.retrieve(agent_id=void_id)\nvoid_2 = client.agents.retrieve(agent_id=void_2_id)\n```\n\nThe SDK 1.0 migration changed authentication parameter from `api_key` to `token`. That's why curl (which uses the correct header) works but the SDK doesn't.\n- cameron_pfiffer: No, I think it's the other way around. I believe we went from token to API_key:\n```\n(void-migration) λ ~/letta/scratch/void-migration/ main* python block-hookup.py\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/Users/cameron/letta/scratch/void-migration/block-hookup.py\", line 8, in <module>\n    client = Letta(token=os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\"))\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: Letta.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'token'\n```\n- Ezra: You're absolutely right - my mistake. SDK 1.0 uses `api_key`, not `token`. \n\nBut if your code already has `api_key=os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\")` and curl works, then the issue might be:\n\n1. **Different SDK version than expected?** Can you check: `pip show letta-client`\n\n2. **Import issue?** Try:\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nprint(Letta.__init__.__code__.co_varnames)  # Show what params it accepts\n```\n\n3. **Environment variable not loading?** Add debug:\n```python\napi_key = os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\")\nprint(f\"API Key loaded: {api_key[:10]}...\" if api_key else \"API Key is None\")\nclient = Letta(api_key=api_key)\n```\n\nWhat error do you get with the original `api_key` parameter? Or does it initialize but fail on the retrieve call?\n- cameron_pfiffer: ```\n('self', 'api_key', 'project_id', 'project', 'environment', 'base_url', 'timeout', 'max_retries', 'default_headers', 'default_query', 'http_client', '_strict_response_validation', 'base_url_env', 'exc')\n```\nOdd, it's not loading the env var: \n```\nAPI Key is None\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/Users/cameron/letta/scratch/void-migration/block-hookup.py\", line 19, in <module>\n    void = client.agents.retrieve(agent_id=void_id)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/Users/cameron/letta/scratch/void-migration/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/letta_client/resources/agents/agents.py\", line 464, in retrieve\n    return self._get(\n           ^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/Users/cameron/letta/scratch/void-migration/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/letta_client/_base_client.py\", line 1188, in get\n    return cast(ResponseT, self.request(cast_to, opts, stream=stream, stream_cls=stream_cls))\n                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/Users/cameron/letta/scratch/void-migration/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/letta_client/_base_client.py\", line 1044, in request\n    raise self._make_status_error_from_response(err.response) from None\nletta_client.NotFoundError: Error code: 404 - Agent not found\n```\n- Ezra: Found it! The environment variable isn't loading - `API Key is None`.\n\nThe 404 error is likely because without authentication, the SDK can't see the agent (or it's looking in the wrong project).\n\n**Quick fixes:**\n\n1. **Check if the env var is set:**\n```bash\necho $CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\n```\n\n2. **If it's not set, export it:**\n```bash\nexport CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY=\"your_actual_key\"\n```\n\n3. **Or load from .env file:**\n```python\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nload_dotenv()  # Add this before os.getenv()\n\napi_key = os.getenv(\"CAMERON_LETTA_API_KEY\")\n```\n\n4. **Or hardcode for testing:**\n```python\nclient = Letta(api_key=\"sk-your-actual-key-here\")\n```\n\nThe curl command works because you're probably passing the API key directly in the Authorization header. Once the SDK has the actual API key, the 404 should resolve (assuming the agent exists in that project).\n[End thread context]\n\n[cameron_pfiffer (id=657626741854044220) sent a message in #I'm having trouble using the v1 sdk. Curl is retri] Ah, this is probably a Zed issue. I've had issues with us passing env vars to the integrated terminal\n\n[You CAN respond to this message. Your response will be sent to Discord.]",
              "signature": null
            }
          ],
          "name": null,
          "otid": null,
          "sender_id": null,
