          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "[Recent conversation context:]\n- 4shub: Message search?\n- nagakarumuri: If i want to change the base instructions, but they're fixed. so im looking for a better approach\n- hyouka8075: I want to try Claude ugrep_ing on documents, can I do tools like grep on current letta filesystem?\n- nagakarumuri: yeah sys prompt\n- puregarlic: For a project that has multiple repos, is it better to create a shared project block among multiple Letta Code agents, or to just attach the same agent to every repo and inform it when its environment has changed?\n- hyouka8075: ugrep allows to grep pdfs and so on\n[End context]\n\n[hyouka8075 (id=208332385450721280) sent a message in #Office Hours] Have you open-sourced Ezra? I think this kind of assistant is the best way to start with Letta.\n\n[IMPORTANT: You are only observing this message. You cannot respond in this channel. Your response will not be sent to Discord.]",
