      "files_agents": [
        {
          "agent_id": "agent-0",
          "file_id": "file-0",
          "source_id": "source-0",
          "file_name": "cameron-scratch/Letta_VAPI_VOICE_AGENT (3).md",
          "is_open": true,
          "visible_content": "[Viewing file start (out of 317 lines)]\n1: # Building a Voice Agent with Letta and Vapi\n2: A complete guide to creating a voice-enabled AI agent using Letta for conversational AI and Vapi for voice infrastructure.\n3: ## Overview\n4: This guide will show you how to:\n5: - Create a conversational AI agent with Letta\n6: - Connect it to Vapi for voice capabilities\n7: - Make phone calls and web-based voice interactions with your agent\n8: **Architecture:**\n9: ```\n10: User (Voice/Phone) → Vapi → Letta Agent → Response (Voice)\n11: ```\n12: ## Prerequisites\n13: ### Accounts Needed\n14: 1. **Letta Account** - https://app.letta.com (sign up free)\n15: 2. **Vapi Account** - https://vapi.ai (sign up, paid service)\n16: ### Tools Required\n17: - Python 3.8+ installed\n18: - Terminal/command line access\n19: - Text editor or IDE\n20: ## Step 1: Set Up Your Development Environment\n21: ### Create Project Directory\n22: ```bash\n23: mkdir letta-voice-agent\n24: cd letta-voice-agent\n25: ```\n26: ### Create Virtual Environment\n27: ```bash\n28: # Create virtual environment\n29: python3 -m venv venv\n30: # Activate it\n31: source venv/bin/activate  # On macOS/Linux\n32: # OR\n33: venv\\Scripts\\activate  # On Windows\n34: ```\n35: ### Install Dependencies\n36: Create `requirements.txt`:\n37: ```txt\n38: letta>=0.5.0\n39: letta-client>=0.1.319\n40: python-dotenv>=1.0.0\n41: requests>=2.31.0\n42: ```\n43: Install packages:\n44: ```bash\n45: pip install -r requirements.txt\n46: ```\n47: ### Create Environment File\n48: Create `.env`:\n49: ```bash\n50: # Letta API Configuration\n51: LETTA_API_KEY=your_letta_api_key_here\n52: # Vapi API Configuration\n53: VAPI_API_KEY=your_vapi_private_key_here\n54: # Will be filled in later\n55: LETTA_AGENT_ID=\n56: VAPI_ASSISTANT_ID=\n57: ```\n58: Create `.gitignore`:\n59: ```\n60: .env\n61: venv/\n62: __pycache__/\n63: *.pyc\n64: ```\n65: ## Step 2: Get Your Letta API Key\n66: 1. Go to https://app.letta.com/settings\n67: 2. Navigate to **API Keys**\n68: 3. Click **Create New Key** (or copy existing key)\n69: 4. Copy the key and add it to `.env`:\n70: ```bash\n71: LETTA_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here\n72: ```\n73: ## Step 3: Create a Letta Agent\n74: ### Option A: Using Python SDK\n75: Create `create_agent.py`:\n76: ```python\n77: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n78: \"\"\"\n79: Create a Letta agent for voice conversations.\n80: \"\"\"\n81: import os\n82: from dotenv import load_dotenv\n83: from letta_client import Letta\n84: # Load environment variables\n85: load_dotenv()\n86: # Initialize Letta client\n87: client = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n88: print(\"Creating Letta agent...\")\n89: # Create the agent\n90: agent = client.agents.create(\n91: name=\"Voice Assistant\",\n92: # Memory blocks define the agent's context\n93: memory_blocks=[\n94: {\n95: \"label\": \"human\",\n96: \"value\": \"Name: Unknown\\nAge: Unknown\\nLocation: Unknown\"\n97: },\n98: {\n99: \"label\": \"persona\",\n100: \"value\": \"You are a helpful AI assistant with voice capabilities. You speak naturally and conversationally. Keep responses concise for voice interactions.\"\n101: }\n102: ],\n103: # Model configuration\n104: llm_config={\n105: \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\n106: \"model_endpoint_type\": \"openai\",\n107: \"context_window\": 16000\n108: },\n109: # Embedding configuration for memory\n110: embedding_config={\n111: \"embedding_endpoint_type\": \"openai\",\n112: \"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"\n113: },\n114: # Optional: Add tools\n115: # tools=[\"send_message\", \"conversation_search\"]\n116: )\n117: print(f\"\\n✅ Agent created successfully!\")\n118: print(f\"Agent ID: {agent.id}\")\n119: print(f\"Name: {agent.name}\")\n120: print(f\"\\n📝 Add this to your .env file:\")\n121: print(f\"LETTA_AGENT_ID={agent.id}\")\n122: # Test the agent\n123: print(f\"\\n🧪 Testing agent...\")\n124: response = client.agents.messages.create(\n125: agent_id=agent.id,\n126: messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello! Introduce yourself briefly.\"}]\n127: )\n128: # Display response\n129: for message in response.messages:\n130: if hasattr(message, 'role') and message.role == 'assistant':\n131: if hasattr(message, 'content') and message.content:\n132: print(f\"\\nAgent: {message.content}\")\n133: print(f\"\\n✅ Agent is working! Ready for voice integration.\")\n134: ```\n135: Run it:\n136: ```bash\n137: python create_agent.py\n138: ```\n139: **Copy the Agent ID and add it to `.env`**\n140: ### Option B: Using Letta Dashboard\n141: 1. Go to https://app.letta.com\n142: 2. Click **Create Agent**\n143: 3. Configure:\n144: - **Name:** Voice Assistant\n145: - **Model:** GPT-4o-mini (or your preferred model)\n146: - **Memory:** Add persona and human blocks\n147: 4. Click **Create**\n148: 5. Copy the Agent ID (format: `agent-xxxxxxxxx`)\n149: 6. Add to `.env`:\n150: ```bash\n151: LETTA_AGENT_ID=agent-your-id-here\n152: ```\n153: ## Step 4: Set Up Vapi\n154: ### Get Vapi API Keys\n155: 1. Go to https://dashboard.vapi.ai/\n156: 2. Navigate to **Settings** → **API Keys**\n157: 3. Copy both:\n158: - **Private Key** (for server-side operations)\n159: - **Public Key** (for client-side, optional)\n160: 4. Add to `.env`:\n161: ```bash\n162: VAPI_API_KEY=your_vapi_private_key_here\n163: ```\n164: ### Create Vapi Assistant\n165: Create `create_vapi_assistant.py`:\n166: ```python\n167: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n168: \"\"\"\n169: Create a Vapi assistant connected to your Letta agent.\n170: \"\"\"\n171: import os\n172: from dotenv import load_dotenv\n173: import requests\n174: import json\n175: load_dotenv()\n176: VAPI_API_KEY = os.getenv('VAPI_API_KEY')\n177: LETTA_API_KEY = os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY')\n178: LETTA_AGENT_ID = os.getenv('LETTA_AGENT_ID')\n179: if not all([VAPI_API_KEY, LETTA_API_KEY, LETTA_AGENT_ID]):\n180: print(\"❌ Error: Missing required environment variables\")\n181: print(\"Make sure VAPI_API_KEY, LETTA_API_KEY, and LETTA_AGENT_ID are set in .env\")\n182: exit(1)\n183: print(\"Creating Vapi assistant...\")\n184: url = \"https://api.vapi.ai/assistant\"\n185: headers = {\n186: \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {VAPI_API_KEY}\",\n187: \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n188: }\n189: # Assistant configuration\n190: assistant_config = {\n191: \"name\": \"Letta Voice Agent\",\n192: # Model configuration - connects to Letta\n193: \"model\": {\n194: \"provider\": \"custom-llm\",\n195: \"url\": \"https://api.letta.com/v1/chat/completions\",\n196: \"model\": LETTA_AGENT_ID,\n197: \"temperature\": 0.7,\n198: \"maxTokens\": 500,\n199: \"messages\": []  # Let Letta handle context\n200: },\n201: # Voice configuration\n202: \"voice\": {\n203: \"provider\": \"vapi\",\n204: \"voiceId\": \"Kylie\"  # Options: Kylie, Emma, Ethan, etc.\n205: },\n206: # Transcriber configuration\n207: \"transcriber\": {\n208: \"provider\": \"deepgram\",\n209: \"model\": \"nova-2\",\n210: \"language\": \"en\"\n211: },\n212: # First message (IMPORTANT: Use static message)\n213: \"firstMessageMode\": \"assistant-speaks-first\",\n214: \"firstMessage\": \"Hello! How can I help you today?\",\n215: # End messages\n216: \"endCallMessage\": \"Goodbye! Have a great day.\",\n217: \"voicemailMessage\": \"Please leave a message and I'll get back to you.\"\n218: }\n219: try:\n220: response = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=assistant_config)\n221: response.raise_for_status()\n222: assistant = response.json()\n223: print(f\"\\n✅ Vapi assistant created successfully!\")\n224: print(f\"Assistant ID: {assistant['id']}\")\n225: print(f\"Name: {assistant['name']}\")\n226: print(f\"Dashboard: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/{assistant['id']}\")\n227: print(f\"\\n📝 Add this to your .env file:\")\n228: print(f\"VAPI_ASSISTANT_ID={assistant['id']}\")\n229: print(f\"\\n🔑 IMPORTANT: Set Letta API Key in Vapi Dashboard\")\n230: print(f\"1. Go to: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/{assistant['id']}\")\n231: print(f\"2. Click 'Edit'\")\n232: print(f\"3. Find 'Model' → 'API Key' field\")\n233: print(f\"4. Enter your Letta API Key: {LETTA_API_KEY}\")\n234: print(f\"5. Save the configuration\")\n235: except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as e:\n236: print(f\"❌ HTTP Error: {e}\")\n237: print(f\"Response: {e.response.text}\")\n238: except Exception as e:\n239: print(f\"❌ Error: {e}\")\n240: ```\n241: Run it:\n242: ```bash\n243: python create_vapi_assistant.py\n244: ```\n245: **Important:** Follow the instructions to add your Letta API key in the Vapi dashboard.\n246: ## Step 5: Configure Letta API Key in Vapi Dashboard\n247: **This is a critical step!**\n248: 1. Go to: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/YOUR_ASSISTANT_ID\n249: 2. Click **Edit**\n250: 3. Scroll to **Model** section\n251: 4. Look for **API Key** field (might be under \"Advanced\")\n252: 5. Enter your **Letta API Key**\n253: 6. Click **Save**\n254: ## Common Issues and Solutions\n255: ### Issue 1: \"pipeline-error-custom-llm-llm-failed\"\n256: **Cause:** API key not set in Vapi or wrong endpoint\n257: **Solution:**\n258: 1. Verify Letta API key is set in Vapi dashboard\n259: 2. Check endpoint is: `https://api.letta.com/v1/chat/completions`\n260: 3. Verify agent ID is correct\n261: ### Issue 2: \"400-bad-request-validation-failed\"\n262: **Cause:** First message mode trying to call Letta before user speaks\n263: **Solution:**\n264: Change `firstMessageMode` to `\"assistant-speaks-first\"` with a static message:\n265: ```python\n266: data = {\n267: \"firstMessageMode\": \"assistant-speaks-first\",\n268: \"firstMessage\": \"Hello! How can I help you today?\"\n269: }\n270: ```\n271: ### Issue 3: Echo - User Transcript Contains Assistant's Words\n272: **Cause:** Microphone picking up speaker output\n273: **Solution:**\n274: - **Use headphones when testing**\n275: - Enable echo cancellation in Vapi settings\n276: - For phone calls, this won't be an issue\n277: ### Issue 4: Agent Not Responding\n278: **Solution:**\n279: 1. Test Letta agent directly:\n280: ```python\n281: from letta_client import Letta\n282: import os\n283: client = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n284: response = client.agents.messages.create(\n285: agent_id=os.getenv('LETTA_AGENT_ID'),\n286: messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello\"}]\n287: )\n288: print(response)\n289: ```\n290: 2. Check Vapi call logs for errors\n291: 3. Verify streaming is enabled (automatic for voice)\n292: ## Customizing Your Agent\n293: ### Update Agent Persona\n294: ```python\n295: from letta_client import Letta\n296: import os\n297: client = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n298: # Update persona block\n299: client.blocks.update(\n300: block_id=\"your_persona_block_id\",\n301: value=\"You are a helpful tutor specializing in physics. Keep explanations clear and concise for voice conversations.\"\n302: )\n303: ```\n304: ### Change Voice\n305: In Vapi dashboard or via API:\n306: ```python\n307: data = {\n308: \"voice\": {\n309: \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\",  # Options: vapi, elevenlabs, azure, playht\n310: \"voiceId\": \"your_voice_id\"\n311: }\n312: }\n313: ```\n314: ### Cost Optimization\n315: - Use smaller models (gpt-4o-mini) for lower costs\n316: - Set `maxTokens` to reasonable limits\n317: - Monitor token usage in Letta dashboard",
