        {
          "type": "message",
          "role": "user",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "user: From: cameron_pfiffer Mentions: iherath7\nContent: Someone else mentioned this, which suggests it's a bug. Thank you for the detailed report!\nassistant: This message does not contain a direct question or issue, so I will not send it to Slack.\nassistant: \nassistant: Tool call returned Sent message successfully.\nuser: From: cameron_pfiffer Mentions: \nContent: I should do a stream on this too, I think a lot of people are interested in digital twins\nassistant: The message indicates interest in digital twins but does not express any specific problem or question that needs to be addressed.\nassistant: It sounds like a great idea, Cameron! Streaming about digital twins could engage many interested viewers.\nassistant: Tool call returned Sent message successfully.\nuser: From: cameron_pfiffer Mentions: \nContent: Hi all, I was wondering why previously connected Remote MCP servers are unable to attach tools throwing the following error: \"There was an error attaching this tool, please try again or contact support.\" also when I try to connect such a server to a new agent it fails after pressing the Test Connection button.\nassistant: Identifying the severity of the problem regarding Remote MCP servers not being able to attach tools and failing to connect to new agents. This seems like an issue that could significantly disrupt operations.\nassistant: Calling tool send_slack_message_to_discord_support\nassistant: Tool call returned Error executing function send_slack_message_to_discord_support: NameError: name 'message' is not defined\nuser: {\n  \"type\": \"heartbeat\",\n  \"reason\": \"[This is an automated system message hidden from the user] Function call failed, returning control\",\n  \"time\": \"2025-08-10 05:13:40 PM UTC+0000\"\n}\nassistant: Searching for potential solutions to the issue of Remote MCP servers being unable to attach tools and failing to connect.\nassistant: Calling tool web_search\nassistant: Tool call returned {\n  \"api_key_source\": \"system_settings\",\n  \"results\": {\n    \"Letta Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error\": {\n      \"query\": \"Letta Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error\",\n      \"question\": \"What are possible solutions for the error 'There was an error attaching this tool, please try again or contact support.'?\",\n      \"raw_results\": {\n        \"success\": true,\n        \"data\": [\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool · Issue #2521\",\n            \"description\": \"Describe the bug Tool created with the error raise RuntimeError(\\\"Something went wrong - we should never be using the persisted source code for MCP.\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521\",\n            \"markdown\": \"[Skip to content](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#start-of-content)\\n\\n[letta-ai](https://github.com/letta-ai)/ **[letta](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta)** Public\\n\\n- [Notifications](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta) You must be signed in to change notification settings\\n- [Fork\\\\\\\\\\n1.9k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\n- [Star\\\\\\\\\\n17.7k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\n\\n\\n# Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool\\\\#2521\\n\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\nClosed\\n\\nClosed\\n\\n[Unexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#top)#2521\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n[Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\nopened [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#issue-2946746710)\\n\\nIssue body actions\\n\\n**Describe the bug**\\n\\nTool created with the error\\n\\n```\\n raise RuntimeError(\\\"Something went wrong - we should never be using the persisted source code for MCP. Please reach out to Letta team\\\")\\n```\\n\\n**Please describe your setup**\\n\\nDocker Compose file with following setup\\n\\n```notranslate\\nversion: \\\"3.8\\\"\\nservices:\\n  letta:\\n    image: letta/letta:latest\\n    ports:\\n      - \\\"8283:8283\\\"\\n    volumes:\\n      - ~/.letta/.persist/pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data\\n      - ./mcp_config.json:/root/.letta/mcp_config.json\\n    depends_on:\\n      python-setup:\\n        condition: service_healthy\\n\\n  python-setup:\\n    build: .\\n    container_name: fast_mpc\\n    ports:\\n      - \\\"3000:3000\\\"\\n      - \\\"5173:5173\\\"\\n    command: [\\\"mcp\\\", \\\"dev\\\", \\\"main.py\\\"]\\n    healthcheck:\\n      test: [\\\"CMD\\\", \\\"curl\\\", \\\"-f\\\", \\\"http://localhost:5173\\\"]\\n      interval: 10s\\n      timeout: 5s\\n      retries: 5\\n      start_period: 10s\\n\\n```\\n\\nA main.py file containing the MCP example code\\n\\n```\\nfrom mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\\n\\nmcp = FastMCP(\\\"Demo\\\")\\n\\n@mcp.tool()\\ndef add(a: int, b: int) -> int:\\n    return a + b\\n\\n@mcp.resource(\\\"greeting://{name}\\\")\\ndef get_greeting(name: str) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    mcp.run()\\n```\\n\\nA docker container that acts as the server\\n\\n```\\nFROM python:3.11\\n\\nCOPY ./main.py /code/main.py\\nCOPY ./poetry.lock /code/poetry.lock\\nCOPY ./pyproject.toml /code/pyproject.toml\\n\\nWORKDIR /code\\n\\nRUN apt-get update && \\\\\\n    apt-get install -y curl && \\\\\\n    curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_18.x | bash - && \\\\\\n    apt-get install -y nodejs\\n\\nRUN npm install -g @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@0.6.0\\n\\nRUN pip install poetry\\nRUN poetry self add poetry-plugin-export\\nRUN poetry export -o requirements.txt --without-hashes\\nRUN poetry config virtualenvs.create false\\nRUN poetry install\\nRUN pip install mcp[cli]\\n\\nCMD [\\\"python\\\", \\\"main.py\\\"]\\n```\\n\\nMCP config\\n\\n```\\n{\\n  \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n    \\\"localTools\\\": {\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"http://python-setup:3000/sse?transportType=stdio&command=python&args=main.py\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nOnce running I executed the following script\\n\\n```\\nimport os\\n\\nfrom letta_client import Letta\\n\\nos.environ[\\\"LETTA_URL\\\"] = \\\"http://localhost:8283\\\"\\nletta_url = os.getenv(\\\"LETTA_URL\\\")\\nclient = Letta(base_url=letta_url)\\n\\nservers = client.tools.list_mcp_servers()\\nfor server in servers:\\n    mcp_tools = client.tools.list_mcp_tools_by_server(mcp_server_name=server)\\n    for tool in mcp_tools:\\n        tool_res = client.tools.add_mcp_tool(mcp_server_name=server, mcp_tool_name=tool.name)\\n        res = client.agents.tools.attach(agent_id=\\\"agent-2ea95cad-1c00-4930-a8ce-369f10d33f0e\\\", tool_id=tool_res.id)\\n```\\n\\n**Screenshots**\\n\\n[![Image](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52256942/426574738-43b29574-3bed-4a8b-9714-9ec1c1065778.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..A_mNR-M5QhvKzK5L_vjxaAQofM-1K63SXtrMwFXKPrI)](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/52256942/426574738-43b29574-3bed-4a8b-9714-9ec1c1065778.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..A_mNR-M5QhvKzK5L_vjxaAQofM-1K63SXtrMwFXKPrI)\\n\\n## Activity\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\n\\nadded this to [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#event-16975883292)\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\n\\nmoved this to To triage in [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Mar 25, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\n\\n[![Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n### Jonathan-Harker commented on Mar 28, 2025\\n\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n[Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n[on Mar 28, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#issuecomment-2762022390)\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\nFixed many thanks\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?s=64&u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4)Jonathan-Harker](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\nclosed this as [completed](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aclosed%20archived%3Afalse%20reason%3Acompleted) [on Mar 28, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#event-17036271066)\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\n\\nmoved this from To triage to Done in [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Mar 28, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8505980?s=64&u=7afb30e3c1bbd65934cfc82e2dbc4f1a5df4d4db&v=4)sarahwooders](https://github.com/sarahwooders)\\n\\nadded a commit that references this issue [on Jun 3, 2025](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521#event-17969267174)\\n\\n[feat: remove in context message reload (#2521)](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/commit/1fc815a185d10e4ed591f446fd92a873977009a0)\\n\\n[feat: remove in context message reload (#2521)](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/commit/1fc815a185d10e4ed591f446fd92a873977009a0)\\n\\n[feat: remove in context message reload (](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/commit/1fc815a185d10e4ed591f446fd92a873977009a0) [#2521](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521))\\n\\n[1fc815a](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/commit/1fc815a185d10e4ed591f446fd92a873977009a0)\\n\\n[Sign up for free](https://github.com/signup?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)**to join this conversation on GitHub.** Already have an account? [Sign in to comment](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2521)\\n\\n## Metadata\\n\\n## Metadata\\n\\n### Assignees\\n\\nNo one assigned\\n\\n### Labels\\n\\nNo labels\\n\\nNo labels\\n\\n### Type\\n\\nNo type\\n\\n### Projects\\n\\nNo projects\\n\\n### Milestone\\n\\nNo milestone\\n\\n### Relationships\\n\\nNone yet\\n\\n### Development\\n\\nCode with agent mode\\n\\nSelect code repository\\n\\nNo branches or pull requests\\n\\n### Participants\\n\\n[![@Jonathan-Harker](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52256942?s=64&u=76a1972a2c184a08a6b4b4906fce5221740b9143&v=4)](https://github.com/Jonathan-Harker)\\n\\n## Issue actions\\n\\nUnexpected code when Attaching MCP Tool · Issue #2521 · letta-ai/letta\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"turbo-body-classes\": \"logged-out env-production page-responsive\",\n              \"language\": \"en\",\n              \"visitor-payload\": \"eyJyZWZlcnJlciI6IiIsInJlcXVlc3RfaWQiOiI2QTM1OjJFQkI4ODoyMTdGNDY2OjJBRDcyODA6Njg5OEQzNEEiLCJ2aXNpdG9yX2lkIjoiODI5ODgwMDQ1ODkzMzc4NTQxOCIsInJlZ2lvbl9lZGdlIjoiaWFkIiwicmVnaW9uX3JlbmRlciI6ImlhZCJ9\",\n              \"octolytics-dimension-repository_network_root_id\": \"703411624\",\n              \"octolytics-dimension-user_login\": \"letta-ai\",\n              \"ogImage\": \"https://opengraph.github