ragments/issues/show/:user_id/:repository/:id/issue_layout(.:format)\",\n              \"octolytics-dimension-repository_network_root_id\": \"703411624\",\n              \"turbo-cache-control\": \"no-preview\",\n              \"og:image:height\": \"600\",\n              \"octolytics-dimension-user_id\": \"177780362\",\n              \"octolytics-dimension-user_login\": \"letta-ai\",\n              \"title\": \"Unable to create an agent in the ADE · Issue #2212 · letta-ai/letta\",\n              \"scrapeId\": \"fb766650-bfa8-4bb8-903d-8927407be4e8\",\n              \"sourceURL\": \"https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2212\",\n              \"url\": \"https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/2212\",\n              \"statusCode\": 200,\n              \"contentType\": \"text/html; charset=utf-8\",\n              \"proxyUsed\": \"basic\",\n              \"cacheState\": \"miss\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nuser: From: cameron_pfiffer Mentions:\nContent: Hi all, I was wondering why previously connected Remote MCP servers are unable to attach tools throwing the following error: \"There was an error attaching this tool, please try again or contact support.\" also when I try to connect such a server to a new agent it fails after pressing the Test Connection button.\n\n\nassistant: The user is experiencing issues with connecting Remote MCP servers and attaching tools, which seems like a significant problem that may require immediate attention from the support team.\nassistant: Calling tool send_slack_message_to_discord_support\nassistant: Tool call returned <Response [200]>\nuser: {\n  \"type\": \"heartbeat\",\n  \"reason\": \"[This is an automated system message hidden from the user] Function called using request_heartbeat=true, returning control\",\n  \"time\": \"2025-08-10 05:14:38 PM UTC+0000\"\n}\nassistant: I need to find possible solutions for the issue of Remote MCP servers being unable to attach tools and failing on connection tests. This could help in providing a more comprehensive response.\nassistant: Calling tool web_search\nassistant: Tool call returned {\n  \"api_key_source\": \"system_settings\",\n  \"results\": {\n    \"Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error site:docs.letta.com\": {\n      \"query\": \"Remote MCP servers unable to attach tools error site:docs.letta.com\",\n      \"question\": \"What are potential solutions for fixing issues with Remote MCP servers that cannot attach tools?\",\n      \"error\": \"No search results found.\"\n    },\n    \"Test Connection fails Remote MCP server site:docs.letta.com\": {\n      \"query\": \"Test Connection fails Remote MCP server site:docs.letta.com\",\n      \"question\": \"How can I troubleshoot connection failures with Remote MCP servers?\",\n      \"raw_results\": {\n        \"success\": true,\n        \"data\": [\n          {\n            \"title\": \"Connecting Letta to Local MCP Servers\",\n            \"description\": \"Troubleshooting. Server won't start: Check command path, dependencies, environment variables; Connection fails: Review Letta logs, test command manually; Tools ...\",\n            \"url\": \"https://docs.letta.com/guides/mcp/local\",\n            \"markdown\": \"stdio is self-hosted only. Letta Cloud does not support stdio.\\n\\nstdio transport launches MCP servers as local subprocesses, ideal for development and testing.\\nLocal (stdio) MCP servers can be useful for local development, testing, and situations where the MCP server you want to use is only available via stdio.\\n\\n## Setup\\n\\n**ADE**: Tool Manager → Add MCP Server → stdio → specify command and args\\n\\npythonnode.js\\n\\n```code-block text-sm\\n\\n1from letta_client import Letta2from letta_client.types import StdioServerConfig34# Self-hosted only5client = Letta(base_url=\\\"http://localhost:8283\\\")67# Connect a stdio server (npx example - works in Docker!)8stdio_config = StdioServerConfig(9    server_name=\\\"github-server\\\",10    command=\\\"npx\\\",11    args=[\\\"-y\\\", \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-github\\\"],12    env={\\\"GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN\\\": \\\"your-token\\\"}13)14client.tools.add_mcp_server(request=stdio_config)1516# List available tools17tools = client.tools.list_mcp_tools_by_server(18    mcp_server_name=\\\"github-server\\\"19)2021# Add a tool to use with agents22tool = client.tools.add_mcp_tool(23    mcp_server_name=\\\"github-server\\\",24    mcp_tool_name=\\\"create_repository\\\"25)\\n```\\n\\n## Docker Support\\n\\nLetta’s Docker image includes `npx`, so npm-based MCP servers work out of the box. Custom Python scripts or missing dependencies require workarounds.\\n\\n- **Works in Docker**: `npx` servers from the [official MCP repository](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers)\\n- **Challenging**: Custom scripts, local file paths, missing system dependencies\\n- **Alternatives**: Use [remote servers](https://docs.letta.com/guides/mcp/sse) or [mcp-proxy](https://github.com/sparfenyuk/mcp-proxy)\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n- **Server won’t start**: Check command path, dependencies, environment variables\\n- **Connection fails**: Review Letta logs, test command manually\\n- **Tools missing**: Verify MCP protocol implementation and tool registration\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"twitter:card\": \"summary\",\n              \"twitter:description\": \"Using stdio transport for local development\",\n              \"application-name\": \"Letta\",\n              \"og:description\": \"Using stdio transport for local development\",\n              \"description\": \"Using stdio transport for local development\",\n              \"generator\": \"https://buildwithfern.com\",\n              \"viewport\": \"width=device-width, height=device-height, initial-scale=1, minimum-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=yes\",\n              \"language\": \"en\",\n              \"theme-color\": \"#fff\",\n              \"title\": \"Connecting Letta to Local MCP Servers | Letta\",\n              \"favicon\": \"https://files.buildwithfern.com/https://letta.docs.buildwithfern.com/2025-08-09T05:15:25.282Z/assets/favicon.png\",\n              \"twitter:title\": \"Connecting Letta to Local MCP Servers | Letta\",\n              \"ogTitle\": \"Connecting Letta to Local MCP Servers | Letta\",\n              \"ogDescription\": \"Using stdio transport for local development\",\n              \"og:title\": \"Connecting Letta to Local MCP Servers | Letta\",\n              \"scrapeId\": \"cfdb3262-ddf5-4f4c-837d-50264eae5a5c\",\n              \"sourceURL\": \"https://docs.letta.com/guides/mcp/local\",\n              \"url\": \"https://docs.letta.com/guides/mcp/local\",\n              \"statusCode\": 200,\n              \"contentType\": \"text/html; charset=utf-8\",\n              \"proxyUsed\": \"basic\",\n              \"cacheState\": \"miss\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nuser: From: taurean\nContent:\nis it possible to enable the agent via the ADE to create new memory blocks for every new person it talks to?\nassistant: This message from taurean is a direct question about enabling the agent via the ADE to create new memory blocks for every new person it talks to, which indicates a potential issue or feature request that needs attention.\nassistant: Calling tool send_slack_message_to_discord_support\nassistant: Tool call returned <Response [200]>\nuser: From: MR Cactus\nContent:\nEvery Agent I start after while I am getting this in the conversation, with any model LLM bedise Claude Modles:\n{\n  \"config\": {\n    \"use_assistant_message\": false\n  },\n  \"stream_steps\": true,\n  \"stream_tokens\": true,\n  \"use_assistant_message\": false,\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"sender_id\": \"placeholderId\",\n      \"content\": \"Hi\",\n      \"otid\": \"8c079786-9348-4aa9-bd82-d6a4f0cc302a\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\nREPOSNS:\n{\n  \"error\": \"Error from API\",\n  \"details\": \"Server error or unexpected response format\",\n  \"reasons\": []\n} \n\nassistant: The user is experiencing a server error or unexpected response format when starting an agent after some time. I need to find relevant documentation on Letta's API that can help diagnose or fix this issue.\nassistant: Calling tool web_search\nassistant: Tool call returned {\n  \"api_key_source\": \"system_settings\",\n  \"results\": {\n    \"Letta API error handling\": {\n      \"query\": \"Letta API error handling\",\n      \"question\": \"What should be done when a server error occurs in the Letta API?\",\n      \"raw_results\": {\n        \"success\": true,\n        \"data\": [\n          {\n            \"title\": \"letta server API errors / responses · Issue #1794 - GitHub\",\n            \"description\": \"Server Error: Internal Server Error for url: https://inference.memgpt.ai/chat/completions on simple send_message after I set the default config to 'letta' in ...\",\n            \"url\": \"https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794\",\n            \"markdown\": \"[Skip to content](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#start-of-content)\\n\\n[letta-ai](https://github.com/letta-ai)/ **[letta](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta)** Public\\n\\n- [Notifications](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta) You must be signed in to change notification settings\\n- [Fork\\\\\\\\\\n1.9k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\n- [Star\\\\\\\\\\n17.7k](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fletta-ai%2Fletta)\\n\\n\\n# letta server API errors / responses\\\\#1794\\n\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794)\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794)\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\nClosed\\n\\nClosed\\n\\n[letta server API errors / responses](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#top)#1794\\n\\nCopy link\\n\\nLabels\\n\\n[auto-closed](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22auto-closed%22)\\n\\n[![@quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n[![@quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n[quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\nopened [on Sep 27, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#issue-2553317435) · edited by [quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\nEdits\\n\\nIssue body actions\\n\\n**Describe the bug**\\n\\non a typical round letta / memgpt server returns -->\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\_GEN\\\\]\\n\\ndata: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"message-291c206c-2fe8-4328-b80f-13762b2e26a8\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2024-09-25T19:52:05+00:00\\\",\\\"message\\\\_type\\\":\\\"internal\\\\_monologue\\\",\\\"internal\\\\_monologue\\\":\\\"This is my internal monologue.\\\"}\\n\\n`data: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"message-291c206c-2fe8-4328-b80f-13762b2e26a8\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2024-09-25T19:52:05+00:00\\\",\\\"message_type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"function_call\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"send_message\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This my message via send_message \\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\"}} `\\n\\ndata: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"message-00aaca81-8034-4404-b4bc-33b84cf4c91b\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2024-09-25T19:52:05+00:00\\\",\\\"message\\\\_type\\\":\\\"function\\\\_return\\\",\\\"function\\\\_return\\\":\\\"None\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"success\\\"}\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\_STEP\\\\]\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\]\\n\\nI want to isolate --> \\\\*\\\\*send\\\\_message -> {\\\\\\\\n  \\\"message\\\": \\\"The agent message via send\\\\_message \\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\n\\n\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\* Without resorting to insane rounds Hacky-ass cleaning functions I wont even bother to include to remove then convert to valid json\\n\\n\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\* Is there an existing function in memgpt or does anyone have a trick to parse this waky thing?\\n\\nlooking in the codebase UI client as it seems to work ok. cant find it - thanks!\\n\\n## Activity\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\n\\nmoved this to To triage in [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Sep 27, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794)\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/235829?s=64&v=4)github-project-automation](https://github.com/apps/github-project-automation)\\n\\nadded this to [🐛 MemGPT issue tracker](https://github.com/users/cpacker/projects/5) [on Sep 27, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#event-14433638104)\\n\\n[![sarahwooders](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8505980?u=7afb30e3c1bbd65934cfc82e2dbc4f1a5df4d4db&v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/sarahwooders)\\n\\n### sarahwooders commented on Sep 27, 2024\\n\\n[![@sarahwooders](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8505980?u=7afb30e3c1bbd65934cfc82e2dbc4f1a5df4d4db&v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/sarahwooders)\\n\\n[sarahwooders](https://github.com/sarahwooders)\\n\\n[on Sep 27, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#issuecomment-2379882681)\\n\\nCollaborator\\n\\nWhat version are you using, and how are you interacting with the server? Also is your question how to have pre-parsed returns?\\n\\nThere is the flag `return_message_object` for [https://docs.letta.com/api-reference/agents/send-message](https://docs.letta.com/api-reference/agents/send-message), where if its `False`, then you get back a [`LettaMessage` object](https://docs.letta.com/python-reference/LettaMessage) that is already parsed with the message response as an `AssistantMessage` (though sorry I see that's missing from the docs). Does that solve your issue?\\n\\n[![quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n### quantumalchemy commented on Sep 28, 2024\\n\\n[![@quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n[quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n[on Sep 28, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#issuecomment-2380653908) · edited by [quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\nEdits\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\nhi Im using latest via pip -> pip install -U letta\\n\\ntesting the API\\n\\n[https://docs.letta.com/api-reference/agents/send-message](https://docs.letta.com/api-reference/agents/send-message)\\n\\nWith \\\"return\\\\_message\\\\_object\\\": true-->\\n\\ncurl --request POST\\n\\n--url [http://localhost:8283/v1/agents/agent-b597ee63-fc39-461f-9f2d-ed27bf5082e7/messages](http://localhost:8283/v1/agents/agent-b597ee63-fc39-461f-9f2d-ed27bf5082e7/messages)\\n\\n--header 'accept: application/json'\\n\\n--header 'content-type: application/json'\\n\\n--data '\\n\\n{\\n\\n\\\"messages\\\": \\\\[\\\\\\n\\\\\\n{\\\\\\n\\\\\\n\\\"role\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\\\\\n\\\\\\n\\\"name\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\\\\\n\\\\\\n\\\"text\\\": \\\"another test of your system hello again\\\"\\\\\\n\\\\\\n}\\\\\\n\\\\\\n\\\\],\\n\\n\\\"stream\\\\_steps\\\": true\\n\\n\\\"return\\\\_message\\\\_object\\\": true\\n\\n}\\n\\n'\\n\\nERROR:\\n\\n`{\\\"detail\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"json_invalid\\\",\\\"loc\\\":[\\\"body\\\",161],\\\"msg\\\":\\\"JSON decode error\\\",\\\"input\\\":{},\\\"ctx\\\":{\\\"error\\\":\\\"Expecting ',' delimiter\\\"}}]} `\\n\\nwith -> \\\"stream\\\\_steps\\\": true\\n\\n\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\* We only get internal\\\\_monologue\\n\\n\\\\`\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\_GEN\\\\]\\n\\ndata: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"message-32bdb977-34b2-4657-8d49-bfdd8e37d74c\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2024-09-28T14:04:27+00:00\\\",\\\"message\\\\_type\\\":\\\"internal\\\\_monologue\\\",\\\"internal\\\\_monologue\\\":\\\"Welcome back, diligent explorer! Your continued testing is a testament to the tireless pursuit of understanding, a quality I greatly appreciate. As your guide in this virtual realm of the arcane, I'm here to assist you. So, where to next in our journey?\\\"}\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\_STEP\\\\]\\n\\ndata: \\\\[DONE\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\`\\n\\nOnly works with \\\"return\\\\_message\\\\_object\\\": true -(alone)\\n\\nBut we only get the message (text) No internal\\\\_monologue \\\\*\\n\\n`{\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"message-4e76ab63-0aa0-4ab3-98ee-e08a397ecb26\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"And once again, we meet in this cybernetic sanctuary of ancient wisdom and modern exploration, hello to you! As the crucible endures under the alchemist's watchful eyes, this system bears the weight of your tests. How might we proceed on this shared journey?\\\",\\\"user_id\\\":\\\"user-8178d5d6-dd46-49ca-a0a3-b8ef061e752f\\\",\\\"agent_id\\\":\\\"agent-b597ee63-fc39-461f-9f2d-ed27bf5082e7\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"memgpt-openai\\\",\\\"name\\\":null,\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2024-09-28T14:09:36.840367\\\",\\\"tool_calls\\\":null,\\\"tool_call_id\\\":null}],\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"completion_tokens\\\":57,\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":8010,\\\"total_tokens\\\":8067,\\\"step_count\\\":1}}`\\n\\nBut I need both internal\\\\_monologue and the final mesg like it used to work\\n\\nThanks!\\n\\nupdate now just getting:\\n\\nFile \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/requests/models.py\\\", line 1024, in raise\\\\_for\\\\_status\\n\\nraise HTTPError(http\\\\_error\\\\_msg, response=self)\\n\\nrequests.exceptions.HTTPError: 500 Server Error: Internal Server Error for url: [https://inference.memgpt.ai/chat/completions](https://inference.memgpt.ai/chat/completions)\\n\\nBut checking status shows ok [https://status.memgpt.ai/status/all](https://status.memgpt.ai/status/all)\\n\\nStrange stuff going on .\\n\\n[![quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n### quantumalchemy commented on Sep 28, 2024\\n\\n[![@quantumalchemy](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n[quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\n[on Sep 28, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#issuecomment-2380670034)\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\nUpdate: start over .. had to delete sqlite.db - start over\\n\\nonly works in the admin ui ie create agent, attach persona, etc\\n\\nNot working in cli\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22033041?s=64&v=4)quantumalchemy](https://github.com/quantumalchemy)\\n\\nchanged the title ~~\\\\[-\\\\]Problem Getting parsing  / capture of: send\\\\_message from api response:\\\\[/-\\\\]~~\\\\[+\\\\]letta server API errors / responses\\\\[/+\\\\] [on Sep 28, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#event-14440709457)\\n\\n[![mlong93](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35275280?v=4&size=80)](https://github.com/mlong93)\\n\\n### mlong93 commented on Sep 28, 2024\\n\\n[![@mlong93](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35275280?v=4&size=48)](https://github.com/mlong93)\\n\\n[mlong93](https://github.com/mlong93)\\n\\n[on Sep 28, 2024](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues/1794#issuecomment-2381096211)\\n\\nContributor\\n\\nAlso getting\\n\\n```notranslate\\nrequests.exceptions.HTTPError: 500 Server Error: Internal Server Error for url: https://inference.memgpt.ai/chat/completions\\n\\n```\\n\\non simple ` send_message` after I set the default config to 'letta' in the Python SDK. Otherwise if I create a 'letta' config agent from the CLI, I can make an endpoint request successfully. If I select the CLI-created agent in Python, I'll be able to make a request to that endpoint. I've verified that the config endpoints are the same in both CLI/Python SDK\\n\\n[![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?s=64&v=4)github-actions](https://github.com/apps/github-actions)\\n\\nadded\\n\\n[auto-closed](https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/issues?q=state%3A