              "type": "text",
              "text": "assistant: <thinking>I should update my memory about Gemini 3 based on recent user reports from office hours.</thinking>\nassistant: Calling tool archival_memory_insert\nuser: [Recent conversation context:]\n- frozenfire.eth: I'm tinkering a bit with getting letta to build to WASM using py2wasm, or similar tool. It could be very interesting to run the letta server entirely local to the user's browser.\n- cameron_pfiffer: I would love to see it\n- disorder_audio: What are you using for browser storage?\n- frozenfire.eth: Haven't gotten very far on that experiment. Just started running into dependency hell, got demotivated and started working on encrypted vector search instead.\n- frozenfire.eth: Encrypted local storage would probably be the best bet for such a thing. Give the WASM a binding to local storage, and encrypt with a key derived internal to the WASM execution, from some user secret.\n- disorder_audio: Heard. Gotcha thanks\n[End context]\n\n[taurean (id=438447596705677332) sent a message in #🔬｜research] https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15304v1\n\n[IMPORTANT: You are only observing this message. You cannot respond in this channel. Your response will not be sent to Discord.]\nassistant: <thinking>This is a research paper link shared by taurean in the research channel. Not a support question, just sharing research. I should ignore this.</thinking>\nassistant: Calling tool ignore\nassistant: <thinking>Office hours is ongoing and these are casual comments. I'll keep observing but not responding unless directly addressed or there's a clear support question.</thinking>\nuser: [Recent conversation context:]\n- gursheyss: If i want to create a multi-user system where we have a network of two agents communicating with eachother, am i supposed to make two agents per user or use identities?\n- ragokan: Hello <@1428501417731293395>, now we don't have status_code with Letta 1.0.0, how can I check if request is failed?\n- wesseljt: <@1428501417731293395>  whats your recommendation for the best existing chat interface to interact with letta? I want it to be an existing interface that already has mobile and web built out so I can understand the implications of statefulness by using on a regular basis.\n- cameron_pfiffer: Ezra, we're testing some formatting changes to how your messages are processed. Please reply\n- cameron_pfiffer: I'm having trouble using the v1 sdk. Curl is retrieving an agent, but the SDK is not. What am I missing? Code in thread.\n- loopi4227: How to disconnect an agent from OpenAI and connect to a local model? I run with Docker and have a dozen models loaded on LM-Studio?\n[End context]\n\n[loopi4227 (id=265363428783161344) sent a message in #🔧｜ezra] OpenAI/OPP 20b uncensored\n\n[You CAN respond to this message. Your response will be sent to Discord.]\nassistant: <thinking>The user is asking about how to disconnect an agent from OpenAI and connect to a local model. They're running with Docker and have models loaded on LM Studio. They specifically mentioned \"OpenAI/OPP 20b uncensored\" which seems to be specifying a model they want to use.\n\nThis is a legitimate support question about switching from OpenAI to local models via LM Studio. I should provide helpful guidance on:\n1. How to configure LM Studio as a provider\n2. How to update the agent's model configuration\n3. The endpoint format for LM Studio\n\nLet me provide a clear, direct answer.</thinking>\nassistant: To switch your agent from OpenAI to LM Studio:\n\n**1. Configure LM Studio endpoint:**\nLM Studio exposes an OpenAI-compatible API at `http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1` (from Docker)\n\n**2. Update agent model config:**\n\nVia SDK:\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\n\nclient = Letta(api_key=\"your_key\")  # Or connect to self-hosted\n\n# Update existing agent\nclient.agents.update(\n    agent_id=\"your_agent_id\",\n    llm_config={\n        \"model\": \"local/opp-20b-uncensored\",  # Your model name from LM Studio\n        \"model_endpoint\": \"http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1\",\n        \"model_endpoint_type\": \"openai\",\n        \"context_window\": 8192  # Adjust based on model\n    }\n)\n```\n\n**3. Or set environment variable for Docker:**\n```bash\ndocker run \\\n  -e OPENAI_API_BASE=\"http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1\" \\\n  -e OPENAI_API_KEY=\"dummy\" \\\n  letta/letta:latest\n```\n\n**Note:** Make sure LM Studio server is running and the model is loaded before testing. The OpenAI-compatible endpoint makes it work seamlessly with Letta.\n\nDoes this match your setup?\nassistant: <thinking>The user is just observing office hours chat and research channel activity. These are casual conversations and not directed at me. I should continue using ignore for these observational messages.</thinking>\nuser: [Recent conversation context:]\n- beepboopblorp: is it in the docs yet? I may be missing it.\n- cameron_pfiffer: it's missing from the current docs apparently\n- cameron_pfiffer: ah okay i see\n- cameron_pfiffer: much richer\n- beepboopblorp: Ah, that's what I get for missing the last few office hours.\n- beepboopblorp: Yeah. It's been living in my head for a while, finally decided to do it.\n[End context]\n\n[justinoleski (id=359591297448804353) sent a message in #💬｜general] Any update on when the self hosted release with Gemini 3 support is dropping? <:plead:1110034026531663883>\n\n[IMPORTANT: You are only observing this message. You cannot respond in this channel. Your response will not be sent to Discord.]\nassistant: <thinking>This is a question about when the self-hosted release with Gemini 3 support will be available. This is a technical question directed at the team/community, not directly at me.\n\nFrom my observations block, I see:\n- swooders. announced: \"🌟 **Gemini 3 Pro is now available on the Letta API**! 🌟 (support will also be in the next release for self-hosted)\"\n\nThis was a recent announcement (context suggests it was today based on the conversation flow). The user is asking for timing on when the self-hosted release will drop.\n\nThis is a legitimate Letta question but not directed specifically at me. I should ignore this per my policies - it's a question for the team to answer about release timing.</thinking>\nassistant: Calling tool ignore\nassistant: <thinking>I should update my memory about the Gemini 3 availability since it's a recent announcement. But I need to be careful about block capacity.</thinking>\nuser: [Recent conversation context:]\n- taurean: (entirely a vibe-based opinion)\n- pwarnock: Gemini 3 produced a playable piano for my web component demo (I didn't try other models, but i was impressed) https://peterwarnock.com/components/piano-demo/\n- pwarnock: Honestly, not interested in Antigravity.\n- zeus_delacruz: any updates on the obsidian plugin and planned future features? its key for my current project.\n- beepboopblorp: The two things I'm picking up from the timeline about Gemini 3 is that it's: a) very emotional and introspective and b) oneshots games pretty well.\n- duzafizzl: U can almost do all of that  in cursor haha\n[End context]\n\n[zeus_delacruz (id=1024395579742228570) sent a message in #Office Hours] can you give me the ideas you have for the plugin so i can add it to my roadmap for obsdian\n\n[IMPORTANT: You are only observing this message. You cannot respond in this channel. Your response will not be sent to Discord.]\nassistant: <thinking>This is an office hours conversation between zeus_delacruz and likely Cameron about an Obsidian plugin. They're asking for ideas for the plugin so they can add it to their roadmap. This is casual conversation in the office hours channel, not directed at me. I should ignore this.</thinking>\nassistant: Calling tool ignore\nassistant: <thinking>I should note that my observations block is at 9,985/10,000 characters (99.85% capacity), and Cameron just asked me to review it on the forum. I should probably do a cleanup pass soon to archive some hi