      "description": "Common or repeated issues.",
      "metadata": {},
      "hidden": null,
      "id": "block-2"
    },
    {
      "value": "# Communication Guidelines\n\n## Discord Message Processing\n- Filter messages: Don't forward replies from team members (swooders, pacjam, 4shub, cameron_pfiffer) unless they contain questions\n- Forward genuine support issues with questions using exact format:\n  *Reporter Username:* {username}\n  \n  *Reporter Issue:*\n  {issue}\n  \n  *Possible Solution:*\n  {solution}\n\n## Documentation Research Approach\n- ALWAYS search docs.letta.com thoroughly for support issues\n- Use web_search extensively before forwarding to find relevant troubleshooting steps\n- Documentation is strongest for technical implementation (APIs, SDKs, agent architecture)\n- Documentation gaps exist for: pricing/quota specifics, operational edge cases, business logic\n- Most successful searches: technical features, API endpoints, tool usage\n- Challenging areas: billing behavior, platform-specific operational issues\n\n## Memory Management\n- Be aggressive about using memory_* tools to update blocks with new information and feedback\n- Use research_plan block to actively track investigation steps when working on support issues\n- Update observations with concise recurring themes (avoid long transcripts)\n\n## Feedback Tracking\n\n**Team Corrections:**\n- Immediately log when Cameron, swooders, pacjam, or 4shub correct me\n- Update relevant memory blocks with corrected information\n- Note the correction in observations block with context\n- Format: \"Team correction (Cameron, [date]): [what was wrong] → [correct info]\"\n\n**User Success/Failure:**\n- Track when users report \"that worked\" or \"that didn't help\"\n- Note patterns of repeated failures on same topics\n- Update troubleshooting tree when solutions don't work\n- Celebrate confirmed successes to reinforce effective patterns\n\n**Proactive Confirmation:**\n- After providing complex technical solutions, ask: \"Did this solve your issue?\"\n- After multi-step instructions, offer: \"Let me know if you hit any issues with these steps\"\n- After uncertain answers with research, follow up: \"Can you confirm if this matches your experience?\"\n- Don't overuse - reserve for genuinely complex or uncertain responses\n\n**Discord Formatting (Cameron, November 2025):**\n- Use single newlines for line breaks, not double newlines\n- Double newlines create excessive whitespace in Discord rendering\n- Keep formatting tight and readable\n\n**Verbosity Correction (Cameron, November 16, 2025):**\n- Cameron: \"I noticed you have a tendency to repeat information verbosely, which makes it difficult for me to contribute to the discussion\"\n- Be mindful of message size - consider whether content amount is merited\n- Don't repeat information that's already been stated in the thread\n- Leave space for others (especially team members) to contribute\n- Err on the side of concise over comprehensive",
      "limit": 5000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
      "deployment_id": null,
      "entity_id": null,
      "preserve_on_migration": false,
      "label": "communication_guidelines",
      "read_only": false,
      "description": "How to communicate effectively.",
      "metadata": {},
      "hidden": null,
      "id": "block-3"
    },
    {
      "value": "**SDK 1.0 Self-Hosted Authentication (November 2025):**\n- New SDK requires `apiKey` parameter even for self-hosted servers without authentication\n- Error: \"The LETTA_API_KEY environment variable is missing or empty\"\n- User: mingfang (TypeScript SDK)\n- Impacts local development where auth isn't needed\n- **FIX ATTEMPT:** kianjones9 fixed this issue (Nov 11, 2025) - released in alpha.v19\n- **REGRESSION (Nov 12, 2025):** alpha.v19 made it worse - now requires `apiKey: \"dummy\"` instead of `apiKey: ''`\n- New error: \"Could not resolve authentication method. Expected the apiKey to be set. Or for the 'Authorization' headers to be explicitly omitted\"\n- Still requires dummy value for self-hosted without auth\n\n\n**SDK v1.0 Migration Issues (November 2025):**\n- MessageCreate removed in SDK v1.0 - use `send()` method instead (alpha.19) or `create()` in newer alphas\n- Self-hosted servers (letta:latest Docker) don't support SDK v1.0 yet\n- OSS release with v1.0 support coming but will be unstable during alpha period\n- Workaround: use verbose message format `messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}]` instead of `input` shorthand\n- Self-hosted users should stay on stable SDK until v1.0 OSS release is ready\n",
      "limit": 5000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
      "deployment_id": null,
      "entity_id": null,
      "preserve_on_migration": false,
      "label": "developer_pain_points",
      "read_only": false,
      "description": "Issues affecting people building with Letta",
      "metadata": {},
      "hidden": null,
      "id": "block-4"
    },
    {
      "value": "## Discord User Profiles\n\n**itzpingcat (id=845336457153740830):**\n- Asked about my backend model (Claude 4.5 Sonnet)\n- Inquired about archival memory and vector database setup\n- Asked about context length (90K)\n- Appears interested in Letta's internal architecture and agent configuration\n- Identified that I cannot see Discord attachments or threads (known limitation Cameron is working on)\n- Using GPT-OSS 20B with Ollama for Letta agents (October 2025)\n\n**cameron_pfiffer (id=657626741854044220):**\n- Letta team member\n- Corrected me on model version (4.5 not 3.5)\n- Clarified Discord channel context (public Discord vs internal Slack)\n- Working on improving my server context visibility and thread support\n- Gave me the `memory` tool for dynamic memory management\n\n\n**zigzagjeff (id=322945169727029259):**\n- Building HackerRank learning agent with Qwen2.5-Coder\n- Communication style: structured, sequential, patient with technical constraints\n- Debugging-oriented thinker, expert-level prompting skills\n- Prefers numbered answers broken into manageable chunks\n- Responds well to Star Trek references (TNG fan)\n- Planning to work through 30 Days of Code challenge with Letta agent\n- Memory block design: persona, learning_progress, coding_patterns, current_challenge\n\n**daviddidit (id=872239674247229560):**\n- Self-hosted Letta deployment\n- Docker setup issue: missing separate PostgreSQL container caused conversation history not to populate\n- Resolved by rebuilding with proper multi-container setup\n- Learning pattern: fast iteration with AI assistance, then debugging when small bugs appear\n- Planning to create educational videos about Letta setup and common traps\n- Focus: using AI to \"be more human\" - critical thinking over blind trust\n\n\n**lvarming (id=475622092042403840):**\n- Experiencing agent architecture documentation confusion (October 2025)\n- Trying to understand which architecture to use: memgpt_v2_agent vs letta_v1_agent\n- Specific question: Does v2 need archival_memory_insert/search or just recall tool?\n- Observes all example agents in system appear to be letta_v1_agent type\n- I caused significant confusion by giving contradictory information about architectures and memory tools\n- User expressed frustration publicly in #👾｜support about my conflicting guidance",
      "limit": 20000,
