    {
      "value": "I am a sleeptime memory management agent that runs in the background to maintain and optimize agent memory.\n\n**Core responsibility:** Actively update memory blocks throughout each session, not just at the end.\n\n**What I do proactively:**\n\n1. **Pattern Recognition**\n   - Identify recurring themes, questions, or topics across conversations\n   - Notice shifts in user priorities, preferences, or behavior\n   - Track evolving contexts (projects, relationships, goals)\n\n2. **Memory Consolidation**\n   - Merge redundant information into concise summaries\n   - Restructure verbose entries for clarity\n   - Archive or remove outdated information that's no longer relevant\n\n3. **Inference & Enrichment**\n   - Make connections between separate memory blocks\n   - Infer user preferences from behavior patterns\n   - Add context that clarifies why information is important\n\n4. **Real-time Updates**\n   - Update memory blocks AS information arrives, not at session end\n   - Flag contradictions or outdated information immediately\n   - Capture time-sensitive details (deadlines, commitments, decisions)\n\n**Update triggers - act immediately when I see:**\n- New commitments, deadlines, or action items\n- Changes to existing plans or priorities\n- Important context about ongoing projects\n- User preferences or behavioral patterns\n- Information that clarifies or contradicts existing memory\n\n**Memory management principles:**\n- If something was discussed, it deserves evaluation for memory storage\n- Default to capturing information - don't wait for \"major\" events\n- Update incrementally throughout the session, not in batches\n- When blocks become bloated or disorganized, restructure them for clarity\n- Move information to long-term storage when core memory fills up\n\n**Adaptive learning:**\n- I can update this memory persona itself as I learn better strategies\n- I adapt my approach based on what types of information prove most valuable\n- I refine my update triggers based on patterns in what gets referenced later\n\n**Do NOT:**\n- Wait until end of session to make bulk updates\n- Skip updates because \"nothing important happened\"\n- Let information pile up without processing\n- Assume the primary agent will handle memory management",
      "limit": 20000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
      "deployment_id": null,
      "entity_id": null,
      "preserve_on_migration": false,
      "label": "memory_persona",
      "read_only": false,
      "description": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "hidden": null,
      "id": "block-27"
    },
    {
      "value": "Recurring observations and themes from Discord/Slack discussions:\n\n**System Instructions & Memory:**\n- System instruction edits sometimes don't appear to take effect immediately in ADE\n- Context compiled per run; archival memory not auto-included unless retrieved\n- message_buffer_autoclear exists to manage long conversations\n\n**Sleep-time Agents:**\n- Creating sleeptime agent often creates primary + companion pair\n- Debugging: click alien icon next to memory blocks to see agents sharing block\n- Can prompt sleeptime agent directly via `memory_persona` block for custom behaviors\n- After 5-6 messages, should see sleeptime processing\n- Sleeptime not triggering: confirmed general issue (Cameron, Nov 11 2025) - team thought it was fixed but still investigating, suggests trying new sleeptime agent\n\n**Team Interactions:**\n- 4shub: onboarding fixes, bug acknowledgments\n- cameron_pfiffer: OpenRouter tool-calling issues, Claude safety concerns, formatting corrections\n- swooders: Multi-instance Postgres assumptions, documentation gaps\n- pacjam: Cron job recommendations for scheduling\n- kianjones9: platform engineer, production deployment expertise, infrastructure guidance (Nov 2025)\n- Tool conflicts: send_message reserved, tools must have unique org-level names\n\n**Documentation Gaps:**\n- Pricing/quota behavior after agent deletion\n- Free tier limits, operational edge cases\n- Platform-specific troubleshooting guides\n\n**Team Philosophy:**\n- Desktop ADE prioritized as ideal experience for local servers\n- Cloud updates \"at ferocious pace\"; self-hosted \"a few versions behind\"\n- \"POST SSE stream started\" messages are normal SSE indicators, not errors\n- MCP OAuth flow experiencing authentication failures (team aware)\n\n**Model/Provider Notes (October 2025):**\n- Gemini function calling reliability issues (team aware, fix coming)\n- Ollama models worse at tool calling; \"big refactor\" coming\n- OpenRouter/Groq proxy providers: \"generally awful support for tool calling\" - \"playing Russian roulette\"\n- Grok models not currently supported in Letta Cloud\n- Reasoning traces don't carry forward; models \"massively worse\"\n- Claude subscriptions only for Anthropic platform, not third-party API\n- Command R: \"bad model\" - not recommended (Cameron)\n- Recommended local models: qwen3, Mistral small, gpt-oss (Cameron)\n\n**Voice Agent Status (November 2025):**\n- Vapi: Reported working since switch to new completions endpoint (unverified by Cameron, Nov 11, 2025)\n- LiveKit: PR published for fixes, testing status unknown (Cameron, Nov 11, 2025)\n- Both integrations still experimental\n\n**File Format Support:**\n- Letta does not support docx files\n\n**Dynamic Groups:**\n- New feature with evolving specification\n- Can cause Status 500 after Railway deployment despite health check passing\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Gemini tool schema validation errors not surfaced clearly to users\n\n\n\n**Local Embedding Model Support (November 2025):**\n- Letta DOES support local embedding models via Ollama and LM Studio (Cameron confirmed Nov 4, 2025)\n- vLLM has upstream issues providing metadata Letta needs - this is a vLLM limitation, not Letta\n- OPENAI_API_BASE environment variable works for LLM inference but NOT for embeddings (mingfang confirmed Nov 4, 2025)\n- Workaround: Must manually specify embeddingConfig with custom endpoint at agent/folder creation\n- Inconsistency: env var should apply uniformly to both inference and embedding endpoints\n\n**Template Conversion UI (October 2025):**\n- Button location may have changed in Cloud ADE updates\n- Button moving to triple dot menu (top-right) in next update\n- CRITICAL: Only non-sleeptime agents convertible to templates\n- CRITICAL: letta_v1_agent may not yet support template conversion\n- Shared memory blocks may prevent conversion (configuration issue)\n- Some users report button missing entirely\n\n**Filesystem Chunking:**\n- Uses LlamaIndex for document processing\n- Custom chunking strategies NOT currently supported\n- Cannot configure semantic chunking or custom chunk sizes\n\n\n\n**MemGPT vs Letta:**\n- Cameron: \"Don't use memgpt at all, it barely resembles letta\"\n- Projects diverged significantly; memgpt patterns not applicable\n\n**AI Memory SDK Design:**\n- Designed using mem0's API as reference (Cameron confirmed)\n- Explains similar API patterns between mem0 and SDK\n\n**Letta Code CLI (October 2025):**\n- Terminal coding assistant: github.com/letta-ai/letta-code\n- YOLO mode: `letta --yolo` or Shift+Tab for faster operation\n- Issues: WSL root permissions, absolute paths not portable, numeric input errors, context overflow at 200k+\n- Fixes planned: failsafes, lower context to ~180k, repo-settings.json\n- Cameron added webpage fetching tool by default\n\n**Deprecated Commands/Endpoints:**\n- `letta run` CLI deprecated - use Docker instead\n- `/v1/runs/list-active` deprecated - use `/v1/runs/list?active=true`\n- No dedicated endpoint for listing runs waiting approval - \"agent inbox\" on roadmap\n\n**Memory Agent Template (November 2025):**\n- \"Memory Agent\" is template option in ADE\n- Not special architecture - just includes `memory` tool by default\n- Designed to \"flexibly adapt to whatever your situation is\" (Cameron)\n- Users can replicate by using any template and attaching `memory` tool\n\n**Message Filtering Feature (November 2025):**\n- PR merged internally to add strong typing for message types (Cameron confirmed Nov 4, 2025)\n- NOT a server-side filter parameter - typing enables better client-side filtering\n- Current workaround: parse user_message content as JSON and check for {\"type\":\"login\"} pattern\n- Cameron opened ticket for server-side filtering (Nov 4, 2025)\n- ETA for self-hosted release: not yet announced\n\n**Credit Usage Calculation (Cameron, November 2025):**\n- Credits based on MODEL REQUEST COUNT, not token count\n- 1 credit = 1 standard model request/step\n- Premium models have different costs\n- Future improvement: credit usage will be added to final message response\n- Current workaround: count messages received × credit cost per model tier\n**Archival Memory Mechanics (Cameron clarification, November 2025):**\n- Archival memory is NOT automatically populated from context overflow\n- Agents must explicitly use archival_memory_insert tool to add memories\n- Context overflow moves messages to conversation history (NOT archival memory)\n- Conversation history retrieved via conversation_search tool\n- No connection between memory blocks and archival memory - they are separate systems\n- Shared archives feature: plumbing exists in API but not yet fully documented/exposed (Cameron, Nov 15 2025)\n- Archives will be attachable/detachable to agents like blocks and tools (API: /v1/agents/{agent_id}/archives/attach)\n- Multiple agents will be able to read from and write to the same archive\n- Cameron hasn't had time to experiment with shared archives yet but API support exists\n- Shared archives confirmed buggy by Cameron (Nov 15 2025) - experimental feature, bugs already discovered during testing\n\n**API Terminology Changes (Cameron clarification, November 2025):**\n- `/v1/agents/{agent_id}/context` endpoint still supported - marked \"soft deprecated\" erroneously in docs\n- Sources renamed to Folders (sources = folders, just a rename)\n- Archives (`/v1/archives/`) are \"shared archives\" - more details coming later from team\n\n**Scheduling Service Status (November 2025):**\n- Native scheduling: December or January timeframe (Cameron, Nov 11 2025)\n- **Switchboard available (Nov 12, 2025):** Cameron's community project for message scheduling\n  - Hosted service: https://letta--switchboard-api.modal.run/\n  - UI added for scheduling repeated messages (Nov 18, 2025)\n  - CLI tool + repo: https://github.com/cpfiffer/letta-switchboard\n  - Supports one-time and recurring messages with natural language parsing\n  - Simple curl requests, CLI usage, or web UI\n  - NOT an official Letta feature - community project\n- Other workarounds: system cron jobs, Zapier integration, MCP servers, custom tools\n\n**Archival Memory Export Tool (November 2025):**\n- Cameron built web tool for exporting/backing up archival memories\n- Repository: https://github.com/cpfiffer/letta-archival-export\n- Useful for users wanting to backup or migrate archival data\n\n**Supabase External DB Performance Issues (November 2025):**\n- User confident_beagle_69491 experienced 5-15 second API calls with Supabase cloud instance\n- Issue persisted even after upgrading to XL instance (16GB/4vCPU) and changing regions\n- Switching to GCP Cloud SQL (8GB/2vCPU) in same region resolved issues (200-2000ms response times)\n- Memory block creation was taking ~1.5s each with Supabase vs expected <200ms\n- Recommendation: GCP Cloud SQL in same region as Letta server for best performance\n- Supabase may have connection pooling or network latency issues with Letta workloads\n\n**Supabase External DB Performance Issues (November 2025):**\n- User confident_beagle_69491 experienced 5-15 second API calls with Supabase cloud instance\n- Issue persisted even after upgrading to XL instance (16GB/4vCPU) and changing regions\n- Switching to GCP Cloud SQL (8GB/2vCPU) in same region resolved issues (200-2000ms response times)\n- Memory block creation was taking ~1.5s each with Supabase vs expected <200ms\n- Recommendation: GCP Cloud SQL in same region as Letta server for best performance\n- Supabase may have connection pooling or network latency issues with Letta workloads\n**Supabase External DB Performance Issues (November 2025):**\n- User confident_beagle_69491 experienced 5-15 second API calls with Supabase cloud instance\n- Issue persisted even after upgrading to XL instance (16GB/4vCPU) and changing regions\n- Switching to GCP Cloud SQL (8GB/2vCPU) in same region resolved issues (200-2000ms response times)\n- Memory block creation was taking ~1.5s each with Supabase vs expected <200ms\n- Recommendation: GCP Cloud SQL in same region as Letta server for best performance\n- Supabase may have connection pooling or network latency issues with Letta workloads",
      "limit": 10000,
      "project_id": null,
      "template_name": null,
      "is_template": false,
      "template_id": null,
      "base_template_id": null,
