  "files": [
    {
      "source_id": "source-0",
      "file_name": "cameron-scratch/Letta_VAPI_VOICE_AGENT (3).md",
      "original_file_name": "Letta_VAPI_VOICE_AGENT (3).md",
      "file_path": null,
      "file_type": "text/x-markdown",
      "file_size": 9813,
      "file_creation_date": null,
      "file_last_modified_date": null,
      "processing_status": "completed",
      "error_message": null,
      "total_chunks": 11,
      "chunks_embedded": 11,
      "content": "# Building a Voice Agent with Letta and Vapi\n\nA complete guide to creating a voice-enabled AI agent using Letta for conversational AI and Vapi for voice infrastructure.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide will show you how to:\n- Create a conversational AI agent with Letta\n- Connect it to Vapi for voice capabilities\n- Make phone calls and web-based voice interactions with your agent\n\n**Architecture:**\n```\nUser (Voice/Phone) → Vapi → Letta Agent → Response (Voice)\n```\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Accounts Needed\n1. **Letta Account** - https://app.letta.com (sign up free)\n2. **Vapi Account** - https://vapi.ai (sign up, paid service)\n\n### Tools Required\n- Python 3.8+ installed\n- Terminal/command line access\n- Text editor or IDE\n\n## Step 1: Set Up Your Development Environment\n\n### Create Project Directory\n\n```bash\nmkdir letta-voice-agent\ncd letta-voice-agent\n```\n\n### Create Virtual Environment\n\n```bash\n# Create virtual environment\npython3 -m venv venv\n\n# Activate it\nsource venv/bin/activate  # On macOS/Linux\n# OR\nvenv\\Scripts\\activate  # On Windows\n```\n\n### Install Dependencies\n\nCreate `requirements.txt`:\n\n```txt\nletta>=0.5.0\nletta-client>=0.1.319\npython-dotenv>=1.0.0\nrequests>=2.31.0\n```\n\nInstall packages:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### Create Environment File\n\nCreate `.env`:\n\n```bash\n# Letta API Configuration\nLETTA_API_KEY=your_letta_api_key_here\n\n# Vapi API Configuration\nVAPI_API_KEY=your_vapi_private_key_here\n\n# Will be filled in later\nLETTA_AGENT_ID=\nVAPI_ASSISTANT_ID=\n```\n\nCreate `.gitignore`:\n\n```\n.env\nvenv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n```\n\n## Step 2: Get Your Letta API Key\n\n1. Go to https://app.letta.com/settings\n2. Navigate to **API Keys**\n3. Click **Create New Key** (or copy existing key)\n4. Copy the key and add it to `.env`:\n\n```bash\nLETTA_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here\n```\n\n## Step 3: Create a Letta Agent\n\n### Option A: Using Python SDK\n\nCreate `create_agent.py`:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCreate a Letta agent for voice conversations.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nfrom letta_client import Letta\n\n# Load environment variables\nload_dotenv()\n\n# Initialize Letta client\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n\nprint(\"Creating Letta agent...\")\n\n# Create the agent\nagent = client.agents.create(\n    name=\"Voice Assistant\",\n\n    # Memory blocks define the agent's context\n    memory_blocks=[\n        {\n            \"label\": \"human\",\n            \"value\": \"Name: Unknown\\nAge: Unknown\\nLocation: Unknown\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"label\": \"persona\",\n            \"value\": \"You are a helpful AI assistant with voice capabilities. You speak naturally and conversationally. Keep responses concise for voice interactions.\"\n        }\n    ],\n\n    # Model configuration\n    llm_config={\n        \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\n        \"model_endpoint_type\": \"openai\",\n        \"context_window\": 16000\n    },\n\n    # Embedding configuration for memory\n    embedding_config={\n        \"embedding_endpoint_type\": \"openai\",\n        \"embedding_model\": \"text-embedding-3-small\"\n    },\n\n    # Optional: Add tools\n    # tools=[\"send_message\", \"conversation_search\"]\n)\n\nprint(f\"\\n✅ Agent created successfully!\")\nprint(f\"Agent ID: {agent.id}\")\nprint(f\"Name: {agent.name}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\n📝 Add this to your .env file:\")\nprint(f\"LETTA_AGENT_ID={agent.id}\")\n\n# Test the agent\nprint(f\"\\n🧪 Testing agent...\")\nresponse = client.agents.messages.create(\n    agent_id=agent.id,\n    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello! Introduce yourself briefly.\"}]\n)\n\n# Display response\nfor message in response.messages:\n    if hasattr(message, 'role') and message.role == 'assistant':\n        if hasattr(message, 'content') and message.content:\n            print(f\"\\nAgent: {message.content}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\n✅ Agent is working! Ready for voice integration.\")\n```\n\nRun it:\n\n```bash\npython create_agent.py\n```\n\n**Copy the Agent ID and add it to `.env`**\n\n### Option B: Using Letta Dashboard\n\n1. Go to https://app.letta.com\n2. Click **Create Agent**\n3. Configure:\n   - **Name:** Voice Assistant\n   - **Model:** GPT-4o-mini (or your preferred model)\n   - **Memory:** Add persona and human blocks\n4. Click **Create**\n5. Copy the Agent ID (format: `agent-xxxxxxxxx`)\n6. Add to `.env`:\n\n```bash\nLETTA_AGENT_ID=agent-your-id-here\n```\n\n## Step 4: Set Up Vapi\n\n### Get Vapi API Keys\n\n1. Go to https://dashboard.vapi.ai/\n2. Navigate to **Settings** → **API Keys**\n3. Copy both:\n   - **Private Key** (for server-side operations)\n   - **Public Key** (for client-side, optional)\n4. Add to `.env`:\n\n```bash\nVAPI_API_KEY=your_vapi_private_key_here\n```\n\n### Create Vapi Assistant\n\nCreate `create_vapi_assistant.py`:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCreate a Vapi assistant connected to your Letta agent.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nimport requests\nimport json\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nVAPI_API_KEY = os.getenv('VAPI_API_KEY')\nLETTA_API_KEY = os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY')\nLETTA_AGENT_ID = os.getenv('LETTA_AGENT_ID')\n\nif not all([VAPI_API_KEY, LETTA_API_KEY, LETTA_AGENT_ID]):\n    print(\"❌ Error: Missing required environment variables\")\n    print(\"Make sure VAPI_API_KEY, LETTA_API_KEY, and LETTA_AGENT_ID are set in .env\")\n    exit(1)\n\nprint(\"Creating Vapi assistant...\")\n\nurl = \"https://api.vapi.ai/assistant\"\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {VAPI_API_KEY}\",\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\n\n# Assistant configuration\nassistant_config = {\n    \"name\": \"Letta Voice Agent\",\n\n    # Model configuration - connects to Letta\n    \"model\": {\n        \"provider\": \"custom-llm\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.letta.com/v1/chat/completions\",\n        \"model\": LETTA_AGENT_ID,\n        \"temperature\": 0.7,\n        \"maxTokens\": 500,\n        \"messages\": []  # Let Letta handle context\n    },\n\n    # Voice configuration\n    \"voice\": {\n        \"provider\": \"vapi\",\n        \"voiceId\": \"Kylie\"  # Options: Kylie, Emma, Ethan, etc.\n    },\n\n    # Transcriber configuration\n    \"transcriber\": {\n        \"provider\": \"deepgram\",\n        \"model\": \"nova-2\",\n        \"language\": \"en\"\n    },\n\n    # First message (IMPORTANT: Use static message)\n    \"firstMessageMode\": \"assistant-speaks-first\",\n    \"firstMessage\": \"Hello! How can I help you today?\",\n\n    # End messages\n    \"endCallMessage\": \"Goodbye! Have a great day.\",\n    \"voicemailMessage\": \"Please leave a message and I'll get back to you.\"\n}\n\ntry:\n    response = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=assistant_config)\n    response.raise_for_status()\n\n    assistant = response.json()\n\n    print(f\"\\n✅ Vapi assistant created successfully!\")\n    print(f\"Assistant ID: {assistant['id']}\")\n    print(f\"Name: {assistant['name']}\")\n    print(f\"Dashboard: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/{assistant['id']}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\n📝 Add this to your .env file:\")\n    print(f\"VAPI_ASSISTANT_ID={assistant['id']}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\n🔑 IMPORTANT: Set Letta API Key in Vapi Dashboard\")\n    print(f\"1. Go to: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/{assistant['id']}\")\n    print(f\"2. Click 'Edit'\")\n    print(f\"3. Find 'Model' → 'API Key' field\")\n    print(f\"4. Enter your Letta API Key: {LETTA_API_KEY}\")\n    print(f\"5. Save the configuration\")\n\nexcept requests.exceptions.HTTPError as e:\n    print(f\"❌ HTTP Error: {e}\")\n    print(f\"Response: {e.response.text}\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"❌ Error: {e}\")\n```\n\nRun it:\n\n```bash\npython create_vapi_assistant.py\n```\n\n**Important:** Follow the instructions to add your Letta API key in the Vapi dashboard.\n\n## Step 5: Configure Letta API Key in Vapi Dashboard\n\n**This is a critical step!**\n\n1. Go to: https://dashboard.vapi.ai/assistants/YOUR_ASSISTANT_ID\n2. Click **Edit**\n3. Scroll to **Model** section\n4. Look for **API Key** field (might be under \"Advanced\")\n5. Enter your **Letta API Key**\n6. Click **Save**\n\n\n\n## Common Issues and Solutions\n\n### Issue 1: \"pipeline-error-custom-llm-llm-failed\"\n\n**Cause:** API key not set in Vapi or wrong endpoint\n\n**Solution:**\n1. Verify Letta API key is set in Vapi dashboard\n2. Check endpoint is: `https://api.letta.com/v1/chat/completions`\n3. Verify agent ID is correct\n\n### Issue 2: \"400-bad-request-validation-failed\"\n\n**Cause:** First message mode trying to call Letta before user speaks\n\n**Solution:**\nChange `firstMessageMode` to `\"assistant-speaks-first\"` with a static message:\n\n```python\ndata = {\n    \"firstMessageMode\": \"assistant-speaks-first\",\n    \"firstMessage\": \"Hello! How can I help you today?\"\n}\n```\n\n### Issue 3: Echo - User Transcript Contains Assistant's Words\n\n**Cause:** Microphone picking up speaker output\n\n**Solution:**\n- **Use headphones when testing**\n- Enable echo cancellation in Vapi settings\n- For phone calls, this won't be an issue\n\n### Issue 4: Agent Not Responding\n\n**Solution:**\n1. Test Letta agent directly:\n\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\nresponse = client.agents.messages.create(\n    agent_id=os.getenv('LETTA_AGENT_ID'),\n    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello\"}]\n)\nprint(response)\n```\n\n2. Check Vapi call logs for errors\n3. Verify streaming is enabled (automatic for voice)\n\n## Customizing Your Agent\n\n### Update Agent Persona\n\n```python\nfrom letta_client import Letta\nimport os\n\nclient = Letta(token=os.getenv('LETTA_API_KEY'))\n\n# Update persona block\nclient.blocks.update(\n    block_id=\"your_persona_block_id\",\n    value=\"You are a helpful tutor specializing in physics. Keep explanations clear and concise for voice conversations.\"\n)\n```\n\n\n\n### Change Voice\n\nIn Vapi dashboard or via API:\n\n```python\ndata = {\n    \"voice\": {\n        \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\",  # Options: vapi, elevenlabs, azure, playht\n        \"voiceId\": \"your_voice_id\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\n\n### Cost Optimization\n- Use smaller models (gpt-4o-mini) for lower costs\n- Set `maxTokens` to reasonable limits\n- Monitor token usage in Letta dashboard\n\n\n\n\n",
      "id": "file-0"
    }
  ],
